COLLDATA("tadabburen","en",[[247,"§Yusuf\ndeeds\nAsk forgiveness from those you have hurt by words or deeds as much as you can, or ask for Allah's forgiveness for them.\nSeek refuge with Allah from satan causing conflict between you and your brothers.\nList some of the favors that Allah, the Almighty, has bestowed upon you, then ask Him to make you grateful for them and give you more.\nguid\nAmong the reasons to be grateful to Allah, the Almighty, is remembering your condition before He bestowed His blessing upon you.\nWhat matters is following Sharia, not how few or how abundant the followers are.\nThe lack of response from those who are being called (to the religion of Allah) is sometimes a test from Allah, the Almighty, to the preacher.\nrefl\nقَالُواْ يَٰٓأَبَانَا ٱسۡتَغۡفِرۡ لَنَا ذُنُوبَنَآ إِنَّا كُنَّا خَٰطِـِٔينَ ٩٧\nWhen they asked him for forgiveness, they reasoned that with an admission of their guilt, as admission of guilt is a pre-condition for repentance. Al-Biqai: 4/97.\nIs admission of guilt a pre-condition for a true repentance?\nقَالَ سَوۡفَ أَسۡتَغۡفِرُ لَكُمۡ رَبِّيٓۖ إِنَّهُۥ هُوَ ٱلۡغَفُورُ ٱلرَّحِيمُ ٩٨\nHe wanted to alert them to the seriousness of the sin, the greatness of Allah, and that he would ask Allah to forgive them at later times. Ibn Ashur: 13/54.\nWhy did Jacob (u) promise his sons that he would ask Allah to forgive them at later times?\nوَقَدۡ أَحۡسَنَ بِيٓ إِذۡ أَخۡرَجَنِي مِنَ ٱلسِّجۡنِ\nHe did not say: \"He took me out of the well\" for two reasons, first: Mentioning the well would demean his brothers and remind them of what they did, so he omitted that part to preserve their dignity. Second: Allah's favor of taking him out of prison is much greater because he came out of the well to slavery, but came out of prison to sovereignty. Ibn Juzay: 1/427.\nIn this setting, Joseph (u) did not mention Allah's favor of taking him out of the well. Why?\nمِنۢ بَعۡدِ أَن نَّزَغَ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنُ بَيۡنِي وَبَيۡنَ إِخۡوَتِيٓ\nThis is an example of Joseph's (u) kind and gracious speech. He did not say, \"satan misled my brothers\"; rather it was as if the sin and ignorance were on both sides. Al-Saadi: 405.\nHe did not say: “satan misled my brothers.” Why?\nأَنتَ وَلِيِّۦ فِي ٱلدُّنۡيَا وَٱلۡأٓخِرَةِۖ تَوَفَّنِي مُسۡلِمٗا وَأَلۡحِقۡنِي بِٱلصَّٰلِحِينَ ١٠١\n(You are my Protector), You are the closest to me inwardly and outwardly. (In this world and in the Hereafter), I have no protector except You, and the protector does what is best for his servant, so bestow your favors on me in the Hereafter more than You did in this worldly life. Al-Biqai: 4/100.\nWhat is the benefit for a servant to be among the allies of Allah?\nرَبِّ قَدۡ ءَاتَيۡتَنِي مِنَ ٱلۡمُلۡكِ وَعَلَّمۡتَنِي مِن تَأۡوِيلِ ٱلۡأَحَادِيثِۚ فَاطِرَ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِ أَنتَ وَلِيِّۦ فِي ٱلدُّنۡيَا وَٱلۡأٓخِرَةِۖ تَوَفَّنِي مُسۡلِمٗا وَأَلۡحِقۡنِي بِٱلصَّٰلِحِينَ ١٠١\n(Cause me to die as a Muslim), when Joseph (u) numerated the favors of Allah, he invoked Him to conclude His favors by causing him to die as a Muslim when his time comes. Ibn Juzay: 1/427.\nReceiving the favors of Allah in this world should not distract one from pursuing His favors in the Hereafter. Explain in light of this verse.\nتَوَفَّنِي مُسۡلِمٗا وَأَلۡحِقۡنِي بِٱلصَّٰلِحِينَ ١٠١\nThe man of truth said: (Cause me to die as a Muslim, and join me with the righteous). Joseph (u) did not ask nor wish for death, rather, he asked that when the time comes for him to die, he dies as a Muslim. He asked for the state in which he will be and not death itself, as Allah ordains. Ibn Taimyah: 4/67.\nDid Joseph (u) wish for death? Explain.\nwords\nآوَىHe took his parents to himself\nالعَرشِThe throne\nوَخَرُّوا لَهُ سُجَّدًاThey saluted him with prostration, as an honor not an act of worship, where it was lawful then\nالبَدوِThe wilderness\nنَزَغَCaused a rift"],[248,"§Yusuf\ndeeds\nReflect on one of the signs of Allah, which you pass by in the morning and evening.\nSay, \"O Allah, I seek refuge in You lest I associate anything with You while I know it, and I seek Your forgiveness for what I do not know.\"\nAfter reading Surat Yusuf, draw five lessons that can influence your life.\nguid\nWhoever calls others to Allah should not seek worldly benefits for his effort, rather he should be keen to receiving the reward in the Hereafter.\nDo not be heedless of the signs of Allah, which are spread in heavens and earth.\nInviting others to Allah with insight is the difference between invitation by the Prophets and their followers, and that of others.\nrefl\nوَمَا يُؤۡمِنُ أَكۡثَرُهُم بِٱللَّهِ إِلَّا وَهُم مُّشۡرِكُونَ ١٠٦\nFalling under those who associate partners with Allah is anyone who assent to the Lordship of Allah and Him being the Creator, but he commits acts of shirk, such as those who worship graves, make vows for them, and believe that the dead can benefit and harm them. Al-Alusi: 13/84.\nHow can a person have both faith and shirk?\nوَمَا يُؤۡمِنُ أَكۡثَرُهُم بِٱللَّهِ إِلَّا وَهُم مُّشۡرِكُونَ ١٠٦\nThey believe in His Lordship but they associate partners with Him in worship. The Prophet (ﷺ) said to Husain Al-Khuzai: \"How many gods do you worship, o Husain?\" He replied, \"Seven, six on earth and one in heaven.\" He asked, \"Which of them do you take account of regarding your hopes and your fears?\" He replied: \"The one in heaven,\" he said, \"If you were to accept Islam, Husain, I would teach you a phrase which would benefit you.\" When Husain accepted Islam, the Prophet (ﷺ) taught him to say, \"O Allah, direct me in the right way and deliver me from the evil within myself.\" Ibn Taimyah: 4/67.\nIt is not sufficient to believe in the Lordship of Allah, His Names and Attributes until one believes in His Oneness when invoking and seeking help. Explain in light of this verse.\nقُلۡ هَٰذِهِۦ سَبِيلِيٓ أَدۡعُوٓاْ إِلَى ٱللَّهِۚ عَلَىٰ بَصِيرَةٍ أَنَا۠ وَمَنِ ٱتَّبَعَنِيۖ وَسُبۡحَٰنَ ٱللَّهِ وَمَآ أَنَا۠ مِنَ ٱلۡمُشۡرِكِينَ ١٠٨\nIt is inferred from this verse that the Prophet's (ﷺ) Companions and the believers who followed him are enjoined to invite others to Islam with every means they have. Ibn Ashur: 13/56.\nThe believer should invite others to the path of Allah with every means he has. Explain.\nقُلۡ هَٰذِهِۦ سَبِيلِيٓ أَدۡعُوٓاْ إِلَى ٱللَّهِۚ عَلَىٰ بَصِيرَةٍ أَنَا۠ وَمَنِ ٱتَّبَعَنِيۖ وَسُبۡحَٰنَ ٱللَّهِ وَمَآ أَنَا۠ مِنَ ٱلۡمُشۡرِكِينَ ١٠٨\nAbdullah Ibn Masoud (t) said: Whoever wants to follow the example of someone, let him follow the example of one who passed away because a living person is not immune to a trial. The Companions of Muhammad (ﷺ) were the best among this Muslim nation; they had the purest hearts, the greatest knowledge, and the least overburdening attitude. They were people whom Allah had chosen to be the Companions of His Prophet (ﷺ), and establish His religion. So, recognize their credit, follow their examples, and hold fast to what you can of their morals and ways of life, for they were on the straight guidance. Al-Baghawi: 4/283.\nWho was the best in understanding the Sunnah of the Prophet (ﷺ), and followed it?\nوَمَآ أَرۡسَلۡنَا مِن قَبۡلِكَ إِلَّا رِجَالٗا نُّوحِيٓ إِلَيۡهِم\nAllah states that He did not send a revelation of law to a woman from among mankind. Ibn Kathir: 3/477.\nInherent nature of mankind entails that male is different from female, and that each is enabled to do that for which he has been created. Explain.\nأَفَلَمۡ يَسِيرُواْ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ فَيَنظُرُواْ كَيۡفَ كَانَ عَٰقِبَةُ ٱلَّذِينَ مِن قَبۡلِهِمۡۗ\nThis proves that Allah becomes displeased with one who turns away from reflecting upon His signs. Al-Biqai: 4/113.\nIs reflecting upon the demise of wrongdoers an obligatory or voluntary for the believers?\nلَقَدۡ كَانَ فِي قَصَصِهِمۡ عِبۡرَةٞ لِّأُوْلِي ٱلۡأَلۡبَٰبِۗ مَا كَانَ حَدِيثٗا يُفۡتَرَىٰ وَلَٰكِن تَصۡدِيقَ ٱلَّذِي بَيۡنَ يَدَيۡهِ وَتَفۡصِيلَ كُلِّ شَيۡءٖ وَهُدٗى وَرَحۡمَةٗ لِّقَوۡمٖ يُؤۡمِنُونَ ١١١\nThe guidance in their stories are the lessons which inspire faith and piety in witnessing the proofs throughout these stories that Allah is governing all affairs, and that piety is the basis of good in this world and the Hereafter. Moreover, the stories of the righteous showed Allah's mercy and protection of them. Ibn Ashur: 13/72.\nList some benefits of the stories.\nwords\nوَكَأَيِّن مِن آيَةٍMany signs\nغَاشِيَةٌAn overwhelming punishment\nبَغتَةًSuddenly\nاستَيأَسَ الرُّسُلُThe Messengers despaired of their people\nوَظَنُّواThey were certain\nبَأسُنَاOur punishment"],[249,"§Ar-Ra'd\ndeeds\nAsk Allah to grant you the reflection on his signs and sure faith in His promise.\nList three benefits of subjecting the Sun and Moon to the people.\nEat two different fruits, then give thought to the difference in taste, even though they are from the same soil and are watered with the same water.\nguid\nTurn to this Quran and grasp its knowledge, as it is the path to the truth.\nThe sign of truth is true evidence, not the number of followers.\nOnly a person who understands can be admonished by the words of Allah.\nrefl\nالٓمٓرۚ تِلۡكَ ءَايَٰتُ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِۗ وَٱلَّذِيٓ أُنزِلَ إِلَيۡكَ مِن رَّبِّكَ ٱلۡحَقُّ وَلَٰكِنَّ أَكۡثَرَ ٱلنَّاسِ لَا يُؤۡمِنُونَ ١\nThe aim of this Surah is stated in this verse, which is asserting that this revelation is the truth and establishing the proof thereupon. Al-Biqai: 4/118.\nWhat is the aim of Surah Ar-Ra'd? What is its topic?\nوَسَخَّرَ ٱلشَّمۡسَ وَٱلۡقَمَرَۖ كُلّٞ يَجۡرِي لِأَجَلٖ مُّسَمّٗىۚ\nAllah mentions the Sun and the Moon here because they are the most visible and moving among all other apparently fixed heavenly objects . Therefore, if Allah subjected these to His power, then it is clear that He has also subjected all other heavenly objects. Ibn Kathir: 3/481.\nThe Sun and the Moon are singled out for mention among all other heavenly objects. Why?\nيُفَصِّلُ ٱلۡأٓيَٰتِ لَعَلَّكُم بِلِقَآءِ رَبِّكُمۡ تُوقِنُونَ ٢\nThe abundance and clarity of the evidence are among the means of attaining certainty in all that is revealed, especially the fundamental beliefs such as the resurrection and the bringing forth of the dead from their graves. Al-Saadi: 412.\nHow can one attain certainty in fundamental beliefs?\nوَهُوَ ٱلَّذِي مَدَّ ٱلۡأَرۡضَ وَجَعَلَ فِيهَا رَوَٰسِيَ وَأَنۡهَٰرٗاۖ وَمِن كُلِّ ٱلثَّمَرَٰتِ جَعَلَ فِيهَا زَوۡجَيۡنِ ٱثۡنَيۡنِۖ يُغۡشِي ٱلَّيۡلَ ٱلنَّهَارَۚ إِنَّ فِي ذَٰلِكَ لَأٓيَٰتٖ لِّقَوۡمٖ يَتَفَكَّرُونَ ٣\nReflecting on these signs leads to the conclusion that since all of them follow this impeccable pattern and consistent course, then there must exist a Capable and Wise Creator Who does what He wills and ordains what He wants. Al-Alusi: 13/127.\nWhat is the benefit of reflecting on the creation of earth, mountains, fruits, night and day?\nوَفِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ قِطَعٞ مُّتَجَٰوِرَٰتٞ وَجَنَّٰتٞ مِّنۡ أَعۡنَٰبٖ وَزَرۡعٞ وَنَخِيلٞ صِنۡوَانٞ وَغَيۡرُ صِنۡوَانٖ يُسۡقَىٰ بِمَآءٖ وَٰحِدٖ وَنُفَضِّلُ بَعۡضَهَا عَلَىٰ بَعۡضٖ فِي ٱلۡأُكُلِۚ إِنَّ فِي ذَٰلِكَ لَأٓيَٰتٖ لِّقَوۡمٖ يَعۡقِلُونَ ٤\n(There are signs), clear evidence that all of these are created by One Who is All-Knowing, All-Capable of doing what He wills from originating, diversifying and innovating the creation. Then, surely He is capable of bringing it all back. Al-Biqai: 4/125.\nHow does growing different plants proves resurrection after death for reckoning?\nوَفِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ قِطَعٞ مُّتَجَٰوِرَٰتٞ وَجَنَّٰتٞ مِّنۡ أَعۡنَٰبٖ وَزَرۡعٞ وَنَخِيلٞ صِنۡوَانٞ وَغَيۡرُ صِنۡوَانٖ يُسۡقَىٰ بِمَآءٖ وَٰحِدٖ وَنُفَضِّلُ بَعۡضَهَا عَلَىٰ بَعۡضٖ فِي ٱلۡأُكُلِۚ\nNeighboring plots of land means close towns sharing the same soil and water, containing plants and gardens yet they differ from each other in fruits and dates. Some are sweet while others are sour. A single branch in a tree may have its fruits differing from one another in size, color and taste, even though the Sun and the Moon are shining on all at the same recurrence. This is a profound evidence of the Oneness of Allah. Al-Qurtubi: 12/10.\nOn the earth there are neighboring plots of land, what is the lesson in that?\nوَإِن تَعۡجَبۡ فَعَجَبٞ قَوۡلُهُمۡ أَءِذَا كُنَّا تُرَٰبًا أَءِنَّا لَفِي خَلۡقٖ جَدِيدٍۗ\nMeaning: This is very unlikely and it is not possible, according to their claim, that after they have become dust, Allah will bring them back to life. In their ignorance, they compared the power of the Creator to the power of created beings. Because they saw that it is not possible for created beings to do such a thing, they thought that it was also impossible for the Creator to do it, but they forgot that Allah created them the first time, when they were nothing. Al-Saadi: 413.\nComparing the Creator to a created being is the reason for the polytheists misguidance. Explain in light of this verse.\nwords\nرَوَاسِيَMountains which stabilize earth\nيُغشِيIt covers\nقِطَعٌDifferent plots of land\nمُتَجَاوِرَاتٌNeighboring plots yet different, some are good while others are not\nوَنَخِيلٌ صِنوَانٌSeveral palm trees growing from one root\nالأَغلاَلُShackles"],[250,"§Ar-Ra'd\ndeeds\nPray in congregation at the mosque, especially Fajr and Asr, as angels take turns and assemble at these two prayers and testify to those who pray them.\nSay the morning and evening remembrance of Allah (Athkar), so that you will be protected by Him.\nAllah's way is to punish a society when a sin has spread therein. Recall a disaster that occurred in a society due to a widespread sin among its people.\nguid\nThe preacher's mission is to convey the message to people, not to force guidance into their hearts.\nThis verse affirms Allah's way that blessings cease to exist when sins are committed.\nIf you want to reform your life and increase blessings and favors of Allah in this life and the Hereafter, start changing yourself by distancing it from sins and sinners.\nrefl\nوَإِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَذُو مَغۡفِرَةٖ لِّلنَّاسِ عَلَىٰ ظُلۡمِهِمۡۖ\nThere He continues to bestow blessings upon them, sending down His kindness and pardon to people when they are still doing evil and their acts of disobedience are still ascending to Him. They disobey Him but He calls them to repent; they commit offences but He does not deprive them of His blessings and kindness, and if they repent to Him then they are His beloved, because He loves those who repent and He loves those who purify themselves. But if they do not repent, then He tests them with calamities in order to purify them from their sins. Al-Saadi: 413-414.\nExplain how Allah's kindness and forgiveness reach His servants despite their wrongdoing.\nوَإِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَذُو مَغۡفِرَةٖ لِّلنَّاسِ عَلَىٰ ظُلۡمِهِمۡۖ وَإِنَّ رَبَّكَ لَشَدِيدُ ٱلۡعِقَابِ ٦\nAllah is the possessor of forgiveness, pardon, and He hides the mistakes of people despite their wrongdoing and committing errors by night and day. Then, He combined this with mentioning the fact that His punishment is severe, so that hope and fear are evenly balanced [in the hearts]. Ibn Kathir: 3/483.\nWhat is the benefit of mentioning His forgiveness and punishment in one context?\nلَهُۥ مُعَقِّبَٰتٞ مِّنۢ بَيۡنِ يَدَيۡهِ وَمِنۡ خَلۡفِهِۦ يَحۡفَظُونَهُۥ مِنۡ أَمۡرِ ٱللَّهِۗ\nMujahid said: Every one has an appointed angel to guard him while asleep and when awake from the harm of jinn, mankind and other creatures except from something decreed by Allah, then it will afflict him. Ka'ab Al-Ahbar said: If Allah did not appoint guardian angels to protect you during eating, drinking and when taking your clothes off, the jinn would have snapped you away. Al-Baghawi: 2/515.\nMuslims believe in the angels and their assigned functions. What are some of the benefits of this belief?\nلَهُۥ مُعَقِّبَٰتٞ مِّنۢ بَيۡنِ يَدَيۡهِ وَمِنۡ خَلۡفِهِۦ يَحۡفَظُونَهُۥ مِنۡ أَمۡرِ ٱللَّهِۗ\nWhen the servant knows that the keepers, angels who record the deeds, are constantly with him, he becomes more cautious of committing sins. This is similar to one who is surrounded by honorable servants of a king, and they are appointed to be with him, so in this case, he would never think of committing a sin. Al-Alusi: 13/143.\nWhen one realizes the presence of angels, how does that affect his behavior?\nوَإِذَآ أَرَادَ ٱللَّهُ بِقَوۡمٖ سُوٓءٗا فَلَا مَرَدَّ لَهُۥۚ وَمَا لَهُم مِّن دُونِهِۦ مِن وَالٍ ١١\n(And when Allah intends for a people ill), a punishment and destruction. (Then it cannot be averted), no one can repel it. (Nor will there be any protector for them besides Him), there is no refuge for them to go to. Al-Baghawi: 2/518.\nCan anyone escape the punishment of Allah?\nهُوَ ٱلَّذِي يُرِيكُمُ ٱلۡبَرۡقَ خَوۡفٗا وَطَمَعٗا وَيُنشِئُ ٱلسَّحَابَ ٱلثِّقَالَ ١٢ وَيُسَبِّحُ ٱلرَّعۡدُ بِحَمۡدِهِۦ وَٱلۡمَلَٰٓئِكَةُ مِنۡ خِيفَتِهِۦ وَيُرۡسِلُ ٱلصَّوَٰعِقَ فَيُصِيبُ بِهَا مَن يَشَآءُ وَهُمۡ يُجَٰدِلُونَ فِي ٱللَّهِ وَهُوَ شَدِيدُ ٱلۡمِحَالِ ١٣\nAs He alone is the One Who drives the rain and the clouds for people, in which is the substance of their provision, and as He is the One Who controls all things, and to Him are subjugated the mighty creations that people fear and are disturbed by, and as Allah is mighty in power, then He is the only One Who deserves to be worshiped, with no partner or associate. Al-Saadi: 415.\nWhat does a Muslim benefit from knowing that the mighty creations are submissive to Allah, the Almighty, and that He controls them?\nهُوَ ٱلَّذِي يُرِيكُمُ ٱلۡبَرۡقَ خَوۡفٗا وَطَمَعٗا وَيُنشِئُ ٱلسَّحَابَ ٱلثِّقَالَ ١٢\nMeaning: Fear of lightening and hope for the rain. When Abdullah Bin Az-Zubair (t) heard the thunder, he would stop talking and say, \"Exalted is He whom the thunder exalts with praise of Him - and so do the angels from fear of Him\"; and said: \"This is a great threat to the people of earth.\" Al-Baghawi: 2/518.\nWhat did the righteous predecessors do when they heard thunder or saw lightening?\nwords\nالمَثُلاتُPunishments of deniers like them\nتَغِيضُ الأَرحَامُWhat the wombs lose prematurely\nوَسَارِبٌHe does things openly\nمُعَقِّبَاتٌSuccessive angels to protect and record deeds"],[251,"§Ar-Ra'd\ndeeds\nPlan today for a good deed -even if small- that will last for you beyond your death.\nFrom the verses you recite, identify an ordinance commanded by Allah and implement it, as a response to His command.\nGive to charity before a day comes when you wish then to give charity but you will not be able to.\nguid\nHearts are like valleys, vary in capacity, and each takes in much good accordingly.\nA rule that never changes: Truth remains even if people think it has disappeared and became extinct, and falsehood diminishes even if it rises and swells.\nGiving examples is an effective educational means which is implemented by the Quran and the Prophet (ﷺ), so work on using the same approach.\nrefl\nوَٱلَّذِينَ يَدۡعُونَ مِن دُونِهِۦ لَا يَسۡتَجِيبُونَ لَهُم بِشَيۡءٍ إِلَّا كَبَٰسِطِ كَفَّيۡهِ إِلَى ٱلۡمَآءِ لِيَبۡلُغَ فَاهُ وَمَا هُوَ بِبَٰلِغِهِۦۚ وَمَا دُعَآءُ ٱلۡكَٰفِرِينَ إِلَّا فِي ضَلَٰلٖ ١٤\nWhoever invokes others besides Allah is like a thirsty person who calls the water from a distance to come to his mouth so he can drink but he is unable to obtain it with his words (through calling), and stretches out his hand for the water but the water never comes to him because it does not respond. Al-Qurtubi: 12/42-43.\nAllah likens the polytheist to a thirsty person. Explain.\nوَمَا دُعَآءُ ٱلۡكَٰفِرِينَ إِلَّا فِي ضَلَٰلٖ ١٤\nBecause of the falseness of those on whom they call besides Allah, thus, their worship and supplication are invalid since the means become invalid if the end is invalid. Al-Saadi: 415.\nWhy is the supplication of the disbelievers in vain? What is the link between the means and the end with respect to truth and falsehood?\nوَلِلَّهِۤ يَسۡجُدُۤ مَن فِي ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِ طَوۡعٗا وَكَرۡهٗا وَظِلَٰلُهُم بِٱلۡغُدُوِّ وَٱلۡأٓصَالِ۩ ١٥\nEverything prostrates according to its situation, as Allah says, (There is not a thing that does not glorify Him with praise, but you do not understand their glorification) [17: 44]. Al-Saadi: 415.\nHow do all things in the heavens and on earth prostrate to Allah?\nوَلِلَّهِۤ يَسۡجُدُۤ مَن فِي ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضِ طَوۡعٗا وَكَرۡهٗا وَظِلَٰلُهُم بِٱلۡغُدُوِّ وَٱلۡأٓصَالِ۩ ١٥\nThe wisdom behind prostrating when reciting this verse is that the Muslim counts himself to be among those who prostrate to Allah willingly, which is a practical admission of his submission to Allah, the Almighty. Ibn Ashur: 13/112.\nWhat is the wisdom behind prostrating when reciting this verse?\nأَنزَلَ مِنَ ٱلسَّمَآءِ مَآءٗ فَسَالَتۡ أَوۡدِيَةُۢ بِقَدَرِهَا فَٱحۡتَمَلَ ٱلسَّيۡلُ زَبَدٗا رَّابِيٗاۖ وَمِمَّا يُوقِدُونَ عَلَيۡهِ فِي ٱلنَّارِ ٱبۡتِغَآءَ حِلۡيَةٍ أَوۡ مَتَٰعٖ زَبَدٞ مِّثۡلُهُۥۚ كَذَٰلِكَ يَضۡرِبُ ٱللَّهُ ٱلۡحَقَّ وَٱلۡبَٰطِلَۚ\nAllah likens knowledge to a water falling from the sky because knowledge revives the hearts just as water revives the bodies. He likens the hearts to valleys since they hold knowledge just as valleys hold water. A heart may hold much knowledge, and a valley may hold much water. Similarly, another heart may hold less knowledge, and another valley may hold less water. Ibn Taimyah: 4/86.\nHearts differ in holding knowledge. Explain in light of the verse.\nفَأَمَّا ٱلزَّبَدُ فَيَذۡهَبُ جُفَآءٗۖ وَأَمَّا مَا يَنفَعُ ٱلنَّاسَ فَيَمۡكُثُ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِۚ كَذَٰلِكَ يَضۡرِبُ ٱللَّهُ ٱلۡأَمۡثَالَ ١٧\nAllah presents an example of the truth and falsehood, and He likens disbelief to a foam on top of a torrent, so it dissipates and becomes stranded by the edges of the valley, then, it is blown away by the wind, and that is how disbelief goes away and perishes. These two examples are presented by Allah: Steadiness of truth, and vanishing of falsehood. Even if falsehood rises to the top in some cases, it will eventually vanish like the foam and residue do. Al-Qurtubi: 12/48-51.\nHow does the Quran present the outcomes of truth and falsehood?\nوَٱلَّذِينَ لَمۡ يَسۡتَجِيبُواْ لَهُۥ لَوۡ أَنَّ لَهُم مَّا فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ جَمِيعٗا وَمِثۡلَهُۥ مَعَهُۥ لَٱفۡتَدَوۡاْ بِهِۦٓۚ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ لَهُمۡ سُوٓءُ ٱلۡحِسَابِ وَمَأۡوَىٰهُمۡ جَهَنَّمُۖ وَبِئۡسَ ٱلۡمِهَادُ ١٨\n(The worst reckoning), Ibrahim Al-Nakhai said: It means that a person is judged on all of his sins, nothing will be forgiven. Al-Baghawi: 2/523.\nWhat will the worst reckoning be like on the Day of Resurrection?\nwords\nبِالغُدُوِّBeginning of the day\nوَالآصَالِEnd of the day\nبِقَدَرِهَاAccording to its capacity\nزَبَدًاUseless foam\nرَابِيًاRising\nجُفَاءًVanished, cast off"],[252,"§Ar-Ra'd\ndeeds\nMaintain ties with one of your kinship by visiting or calling.\nGive two alms in charity for the sake of Allah, one in secret and the other in public.\nThink of someone who wronged you and send him a good-hearted message or a gift.\nguid\nPatience can come from both the righteous and the wicked, but rewarded patience is that which seeks the pleasure of Allah, the Almighty.\nNot everything which brings you pleasure in this life will benefit you in the Hereafter.\nExtension of provision or its restriction is not a sign of Allah's pleasure or wrath with His servant.\nrefl\nإِنَّمَا يَتَذَكَّرُ أُوْلُواْ ٱلۡأَلۡبَٰبِ ١٩ ٱلَّذِينَ يُوفُونَ بِعَهۡدِ ٱللَّهِ وَلَا يَنقُضُونَ ٱلۡمِيثَٰقَ ٢٠\nMeaning: The covenant that they made with Allah and by which they are bound, which includes all the covenants, promises, vows and oaths that people make. No servant can be regarded as one of the people of understanding who will have that great reward unless he fulfills his covenants completely and perfectly, without undermining or diminishing them. Al-Saadi: 416\nWhen is a servant considered to be among the people of understanding?\nوَيَدۡرَءُونَ بِٱلۡحَسَنَةِ ٱلسَّيِّئَةَ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ لَهُمۡ عُقۡبَى ٱلدَّارِ ٢٢\nIt is said that they ward off those who wronged them with good; but it is more probably that they do good to prevent evil, as Allah says, (Indeed, good deeds wipe out evil deeds) [11:114]. Ibn Juzay: 1/436.\nAllah opens a door for His servants to ward off evil. What is it?\nجَنَّٰتُ عَدۡنٖ يَدۡخُلُونَهَا وَمَن صَلَحَ مِنۡ ءَابَآئِهِمۡ وَأَزۡوَٰجِهِمۡ وَذُرِّيَّٰتِهِمۡۖ\nAllah will gather them with their loved ones, parents, family members and offspring, those who are righteous and deserve to enter Paradise, so that their eyes are comforted by seeing them. Ibn Kathir: 3/492.\nAllah will gather parents, spouses and righteous offspring in Paradise. Why?\nوَٱلۡمَلَٰٓئِكَةُ يَدۡخُلُونَ عَلَيۡهِم مِّن كُلِّ بَابٖ ٢٣ سَلَٰمٌ عَلَيۡكُم بِمَا صَبَرۡتُمۡۚ فَنِعۡمَ عُقۡبَى ٱلدَّارِ ٢٤\n(And the angels will enter upon them from every gate), this is a more encouraging feature of Paradise because having the King's Messengers frequently coming is more pleasing and a sign of high honor. Al-Biqai: 4/147.\nWhat is the benefit of the entrance of angels upon the believers in Paradise?\nٱللَّهُ يَبۡسُطُ ٱلرِّزۡقَ لِمَن يَشَآءُ وَيَقۡدِرُۚ وَفَرِحُواْ بِٱلۡحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنۡيَا وَمَا ٱلۡحَيَوٰةُ ٱلدُّنۡيَا فِي ٱلۡأٓخِرَةِ إِلَّا مَتَٰعٞ ٢٦\nThe extension of provision is not a sign of honoring them [the disbelievers], just as restricting of provision for some believers is not a sign of humiliation. Both situations stem from the divine wisdom known by Allah, the Almighty. He may extends the disbeliever's provision to gradually lead him to his destruction, while, He restricts the believer's provision to increase his reward. Al-Alusi: 13/184.\nIs the extension of one's provision in this life a sign of his success and honor?\nوَفَرِحُواْ بِٱلۡحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنۡيَا\nA rejoice which makes them feel content with it to the extent that they neglect the Hereafter, and that is due to their lack of reason. Al-Saadi: 417.\nWhen is the rejoice in the life of this world censured?\nٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ وَتَطۡمَئِنُّ قُلُوبُهُم بِذِكۡرِ ٱللَّهِۗ أَلَا بِذِكۡرِ ٱللَّهِ تَطۡمَئِنُّ ٱلۡقُلُوبُ ٢٨\nEvery heart is assured by the remembrance of Allah, and if any one denies that, he is a liar and a stubborn. Whoever submits [to Allah] and does good accordingly, is a believer. Al-Biqai: 4/147.\nWhat keeps the hearts from being fully assured?\nwords\nالأَلبَابِUnderstanding minds\nالمِيثَاقَThe confirmed covenant\nوَيَدرَأُونThey ward off\nعُقبى الدَّارِThe good final abod\nوَيَقدِرُHe restricts\nمَتَاعٌA little and brief enjoyment"],[253,"§Ar-Ra'd\ndeeds\nSupplicate Allah to grant you a good life and a good return.\nWhen you wake up in the morning, say, \"Allah suffices me, there is none worthy of worship but Him. I have placed my trust in Him, He is the Lord of the Majestic Throne.\"\nWhen you leave your house, say, \"In the name of Allah, I have placed my trust in Him; there is no power nor strength except in Allah.\"\nguid\nIf you come across someone who mocks your steadfastness in faith, then pay no attention to his ignorance. Do not grieve, be certain that Allah will help you overcome your enemy, and know that your Prophet (ﷺ) endured much more, so be patient for the sake of Allah, the Almighty.\nMisfortunes can sometimes be due to sins, so avoid sins and, Allah willing, you will be happy in your life.\nBe certain that liars, oppressors and disobedient people, even if they are proud and tyrant and seem happy, are actually in torment. How can they be happy when Allah has threatened them with torment in this worldly life?\nrefl\nوَهُمۡ يَكۡفُرُونَ بِٱلرَّحۡمَٰنِۚ\n(In the Most Merciful), indicates His great forbearance and lengthy deliberateness, and it is a clear censure for their attitudes in countering Allah’s favors with ingratitude and denial while claiming to be the most grateful among all people. Al-Biqai: 4/151.\nThere is a lesson in using Allah's Name (the Most Merciful) in this verse. What is it?\nقُلۡ هُوَ رَبِّي لَآ إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا هُوَ عَلَيۡهِ تَوَكَّلۡتُ وَإِلَيۡهِ مَتَابِ ٣٠\nThe repentant return to Allah is through worship, obedience to Him and His Messenger. The servant is not considered to be obedient to Allah and His Messenger -let alone be among the special allies of Allah- unless he does what Allah enjoins, and abstains from what He forbids. Ibn Taimyah: 4/93.\nWhat is meant by the repentant return to Allah?\nقُلۡ هُوَ رَبِّي لَآ إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا هُوَ عَلَيۡهِ تَوَكَّلۡتُ وَإِلَيۡهِ مَتَابِ ٣٠\n(And to Him is my repentant return), meaning: I repent to Him; as Allah says, (ask forgiveness for your sin) [47:19]. The Prophet (ﷺ) was enjoined by Allah to repent, which indicates the virtue of repentance, its significance to Allah, and the fact that it is a trait of the Prophets. Al-Alusi: 13/193.\nThis verse indicates a trait of the Prophets, what is it?\nأَفَلَمۡ يَاْيۡـَٔسِ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوٓاْ أَن لَّوۡ يَشَآءُ ٱللَّهُ لَهَدَى ٱلنَّاسَ جَمِيعٗاۗ\nDo the believers not know that if Allah had willed, He could have guided all the people without the need for them to witness the signs? Moreover, it is said: Do the believers not despair that the disbelievers will ever accept the faith? Knowing that if Allah had willed, He could have guided them; since the believers were eager to have the disbelievers accept the faith, they wished for the coming of the signs suggested by the disbelievers. Al-Shawkani : 3/101.\nA preacher conveys the message and shows the way, but the results rest with Allah's knowledge and wisdom. Explain in light of this verse.\nوَلَقَدِ ٱسۡتُهۡزِئَ بِرُسُلٖ مِّن قَبۡلِكَ فَأَمۡلَيۡتُ لِلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ\nMeaning: I granted them respite until they thought that they would not be punished. So, these people who disbelieve in you and ridicule you should not be deceived because of Our respite, for they have an example in the nations who came before them. So, let them beware, lest the same fate befall them as befell those people. Al-Saadi: 418.\nWhat is the risk for one who feel secure from punishment while committing sins?\nأَفَمَنۡ هُوَ قَآئِمٌ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ نَفۡسِۢ بِمَا كَسَبَتۡۗ\nHe is Allah, the All-Preserver, the Ever-Watchful of the deeds of each one. Meaning: Is He who is the maintainer of every soul, [knowing] what it has earned worthy of worship or someone else? Ibn Juzay: 1/438.\nThe attentiveness of Allah includes several meanings and traits. What are they?\nوَجَعَلُواْ لِلَّهِ شُرَكَآءَ قُلۡ سَمُّوهُمۡۚ\n(Say, \"Name them\"), by their real names, as when they do and their truth is revealed that they are mere stone, or similar helpless inanimate objects, then the foolishness of their minds and the absurdity of their beliefs will be known. Al-Biqai: 4/155.\nWhat is the wisdom behind asking the disbelievers to name their idols?\nwords\nطُوبَى لَهُمA good state is theirs, a comfort to the eye\nقَارِعَةA calamity\nفَأَملَيتُI gave them respite\nأَم بِظَاهِرٍ مِن القَولِYou call them partners apparently without truth"],[254,"§Ar-Ra'd\ndeeds\nRecall from memory verses from the Quran that Allah had made easy for you to memorize, or reflect on their meanings. Be pleased with that and thank Allah for this goodness.\nAsk Allah to make your heart firm upon His religion, and seek refuge with Him from following the desires of those who are not certain in faith.\nAsk Allah to increase the number of scholars and their students among Muslims, and that He gives them a long life.\nguid\nit is important to learn Arabic language and promote its spread because it is the foundation of understanding the Quran.\nBeware of listening and snatching the doubts which are cast by the disbelievers, for the consequence of that is that Allah will forsake you because you turned away from His Sharia.\nStrive to convey the message of Allah to people; as for their guidance, it is in the Hand of Allah, the Almighty.\nrefl\nمَّثَلُ ٱلۡجَنَّةِ ٱلَّتِي وُعِدَ ٱلۡمُتَّقُونَۖ تَجۡرِي مِن تَحۡتِهَا ٱلۡأَنۡهَٰرُۖ أُكُلُهَا دَآئِمٞ وَظِلُّهَاۚ\n(Its fruit is eternal), its fruits and bliss do not cease. (So is its shade), its shade is deepened and does not recede. Al-Baghawi: 2/535.\nWhat are the features of the fruits and shade in Paradise which are mentioned in this verse?\nوَٱلَّذِينَ ءَاتَيۡنَٰهُمُ ٱلۡكِتَٰبَ يَفۡرَحُونَ بِمَآ أُنزِلَ إِلَيۡكَۖ وَمِنَ ٱلۡأَحۡزَابِ مَن يُنكِرُ بَعۡضَهُۥۚ قُلۡ إِنَّمَآ أُمِرۡتُ أَنۡ أَعۡبُدَ ٱللَّهَ وَلَآ أُشۡرِكَ بِهِۦٓۚ إِلَيۡهِ أَدۡعُواْ وَإِلَيۡهِ مَـَٔابِ ٣٦\n(Say, \"I have only been commanded to worship Allah), this verse is related to what preceded it, which comes as a response to the deniers as if saying to them: I have only been commanded to worship Allah and affirm His Oneness, so how can you deny that? Ibn Juzay: 1/438.\nThe Quran ordains a command which coincides with the natural disposition of mankind. What is it?\nقُلۡ إِنَّمَآ أُمِرۡتُ أَنۡ أَعۡبُدَ ٱللَّهَ وَلَآ أُشۡرِكَ بِهِۦٓۚ\nThe eloquence of the Quran is visible in this verse by gradually affirming the Oneness of Allah. Allah says, (to worship Allah), since none of the people of Book would argue with that. Then, comes, (and associate none with Him) to nullify the shirk of the polytheists, and allude to negating the divinity of Jesus (u). Ibn Ashur: 13/158.\nThis Quran gradually affirms the Oneness of Allah and nullifies shirk. Explain.\nوَكَذَٰلِكَ أَنزَلۡنَٰهُ حُكۡمًا عَرَبِيّٗاۚ\nThe Quran has two perfections: A perfection of its meanings and aims in being a legislation, and a perfection of its words in being in Arabic. Ibn Ashur: 13/160.\nThis verse mentions two perfections of the Holy Quran. What are they?\nوَلَئِنِ ٱتَّبَعۡتَ أَهۡوَآءَهُم بَعۡدَ مَا جَآءَكَ مِنَ ٱلۡعِلۡمِ مَا لَكَ مِنَ ٱللَّهِ مِن وَلِيّٖ وَلَا وَاقٖ ٣٧\n(And if you should follow their inclinations), which means following the desires of polytheists in worshiping others beside Allah. (You would not have against Allah any ally) means: you will have no helper to support you. (Or any protector) to protect you against Allah's punishment. This speech is directed to the Prophet (ﷺ), but intended for all Muslims. Al-Qurtubi: 12/84.\nWhat is the punishment and recompense of those who follow the desires of disbelievers from east and west?\nيَمۡحُواْ ٱللَّهُ مَا يَشَآءُ وَيُثۡبِتُۖ وَعِندَهُۥٓ أُمُّ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ ٣٩\n(Allah), the Greatest King. (Eliminates what He wills), the elimination of some Sharia rulings and other things through abrogation. (Or confirms) whatever He wills by affirming and decreeing. All of that follow the best interests that are suitable for each period of time, as He is the All-Knowing, the Effecter of what He intends and none can object to Him. Al-Biqai: 4/160.\nWhat is the wisdom behind abrogating some of Sharia rulings and affirming others?\nأَوَ لَمۡ يَرَوۡاْ أَنَّا نَأۡتِي ٱلۡأَرۡضَ نَنقُصُهَا مِنۡ مِنۡ أَطۡرَافِهَاۚ\nThe diminishing of the land is due to what is conquered by Muslims from disbelievers' land, which means: Do the disbelievers not see that, and be concerned that We should make you overpower them. Moreover, it is said that the land means the whole earth, and that it is diminished through the death of its inhabitants, the destruction of its crops and the ruining of its communities. Ibn Juzay: 1/439.\nDiminishing the land from its sides has several meanings. Explain.\nwords\nأُكُلُهَاIts fruits\nعُقبَىThe consequence\nالأَحزَابِThe disbelieving factions\nنَنقُصُهَا مِن أَطرَافِهَاMuslims conquering polytheists’ lands\nلا مُعَقِّبَThere is none to change or nullifies"],[255,"§Ar-Ra'd, Ibrahim\ndeeds\nIn the morning and evening, repeat this supplication three times: \"I am pleased with Allah as my Lord, with Islam as my religion, and with Muhammad (ﷺ) as my Prophet.\"\nRead a Surah from the Quran, and draw its lessons to enlighten your path.\nRecall days of hardship through which the community went, and work with those around you to draw lessons from that event, then share them with people you know.\nguid\nIf you have doubts about a certain matter and did not know the truth, then hasten to read the Holy Quran, so that Allah may guide you to truth and the right course.\nGuidance comes only by Allah's permission and help.\nAmong the features of Sharia is easing the process of learning and understanding.\nrefl\nقُلۡ كَفَىٰ بِٱللَّهِ شَهِيدَۢا بَيۡنِي وَبَيۡنَكُمۡ وَمَنۡ عِندَهُۥ عِلۡمُ ٱلۡكِتَٰبِ ٤٣\nThe only reason why Allah said that the testimony of the People of the Scripture should be sought is because they are people who have knowledge of this matter, and testimony is only to be sought from people who have more knowledge of the matter than others. This is in contrast to those who have nothing to do with it, such as the illiterate polytheist Arabs and others; there was no benefit in seeking their testimony since they had no experience or knowledge of the matter. Al-Saadi: 420-421.\nAllah said that the testimony of the People of the Scripture should be sought. Why?\nكِتَٰبٌ أَنزَلۡنَٰهُ إِلَيۡكَ لِتُخۡرِجَ ٱلنَّاسَ مِنَ ٱلظُّلُمَٰتِ إِلَى ٱلنُّورِ بِإِذۡنِ رَبِّهِمۡ\n(So that you may bring people) by the book, which is the Quran. (Out of darkness into the light) from the darkness of disbelief, misguidance and ignorance into the light of faith and knowledge. That is likening disbelief to darkness and Islam to the light. Al-Qurtubi: 12/102.\nFor one who wants to rid of darkness in his heart and receive the light, what should he do?\nإِلَىٰ صِرَٰطِ ٱلۡعَزِيزِ ٱلۡحَمِيدِ ١\nMentioning (the All-Mighty, the Praiseworthy) after mentioning the path that leads to Him indicates that the one who follows this path will be honored and protected by the might of Allah, even if he has no supporters except Him, and he will have a good outcome in all of his affairs. Al-Saadi: 421.\nWhat is the benefit of associating the path to Allah's Holy Names: (the All-Mighty) , (the Praiseworthy)?\nٱلَّذِينَ يَسۡتَحِبُّونَ ٱلۡحَيَوٰةَ ٱلدُّنۡيَا عَلَى ٱلۡأٓخِرَةِ وَيَصُدُّونَ عَن سَبِيلِ ٱللَّهِ وَيَبۡغُونَهَا عِوَجًاۚ أُوْلَٰٓئِكَ فِي ضَلَٰلِۢ بَعِيدٖ ٣\nThis meaning of this verse applies to whoever prefers the life of this world and its adornments, chooses its enjoyments over the bliss of the Hereafter, and averts people from the way of Allah. In an authentic Hadith, the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \"I only fear for my Ummah from the misguiding leaders.\" They are in abundance these days, and we seek Allah's help. Moreover, it is said that (those who prefer) means those who pursue unlawful gains of this life. Al-Qurtubi: 12/104.\nWhat are the traits of those rebuked by Allah in this verse so that we may avoid them?\nوَمَآ أَرۡسَلۡنَا مِن رَّسُولٍ إِلَّا بِلِسَانِ قَوۡمِهِۦ\nThis verse is quoted as evidence that acquiring knowledge of the Arabic language which leads to understanding the words of Allah and His Messenger (ﷺ) is required and is dear to Allah because knowledge of what He revealed to His Messenger (ﷺ) cannot be attained otherwise. Al-Saadi: 421.\nAcquiring knowledge of the Arabic language is important. How do we infer that from this verse?\nوَذَكِّرۡهُم بِأَيَّىٰمِ ٱللَّهِۚ إِنَّ فِي ذَٰلِكَ لَأٓيَٰتٖ لِّكُلِّ صَبَّارٖ شَكُورٖ ٥\n(And remind them of the days of Allah) means: His punishment of previous generations. Also, it is said His favors upon the Children of Israel. The term, (Days of Allah) includes both His favors and punishments. The word (days) is used to indicate its occurrence over days, which is also a way of honoring these days, as one would say: The day of such and such. Ibn Juzay: 1/441.\nReading the history of passed generations can strengthen the faith. Explain.\nوَذَكِّرۡهُم بِأَيَّىٰمِ ٱللَّهِۚ إِنَّ فِي ذَٰلِكَ لَأٓيَٰتٖ لِّكُلِّ صَبَّارٖ شَكُورٖ ٥\nIn different verses of the Quran, Allah says, (Indeed in that are signs for everyone patient and grateful), patience and gratitude in response to what Allah decrees upon His servant of ease and hardship, prosperity and adversity, and the good deeds and misdeeds. The servant should receive adversities with patience, and be grateful for prosperities. Doing good deeds is part of Allah's favors upon His servants while other favors are the consequences of his deeds. Ibn Taimyah: 4/107.\nThe believer should deal with Allah's decree by patience and gratitude. Explain.\nwords\nوَيَبغُونَهَا عِوَجًاThey seek to make it crooked\nبِأَيَّامِ اللهِAllah's favors and punishments"],[256,"§Ibrahim\ndeeds\nReflect on the dialogue of the Messengers with their people and draw three lessons to help you follow their example when engaging in a dialogue.\nList five of the greatest favors bestowed upon you by Allah today, and thank Him much for them, then say, \"O Allah, whatever blessing has been received by me or any one of Your creation, it is from You alone, You have no partner. All praise is for You and thanks to You.\"\nShare a message in which you remind others to be grateful for Allah's favors, and warn from their cease.\nguid\nUngratefulness for Allah's favors is a reason for their cease.\nOffering gratitude for Allah's favors by words, heart and action is a reason for their increase.\nA preacher should have confidence in his speech so it has a positive effect on the listeners.\nrefl\nإِذۡ أَنجَىٰكُم مِّنۡ ءَالِ فِرۡعَوۡنَ يَسُومُونَكُمۡ سُوٓءَ ٱلۡعَذَابِ وَيُذَبِّحُونَ أَبۡنَآءَكُمۡ وَيَسۡتَحۡيُونَ نِسَآءَكُمۡۚ وَفِي ذَٰلِكُم بَلَآءٞ مِّن رَّبِّكُمۡ عَظِيمٞ ٦\nA trial means a test, and the trial here is by a disaster, and it is a test for patience. Ibn Ashur: 13/192.\nWhat is the aim of a trial?\nوَإِذۡ تَأَذَّنَ رَبُّكُمۡ لَئِن شَكَرۡتُمۡ لَأَزِيدَنَّكُمۡۖ وَلَئِن كَفَرۡتُمۡ إِنَّ عَذَابِي لَشَدِيدٞ ٧\nIf you are grateful) for My blessings (I will surely give you more) of My favors. Al-Hasan said: (If you are grateful) for my blessings (I will surely give you more) ways to My obedience. Ibn Abbas (k) explained by saying: If you submit to My Oneness and obedience, I will reward you more. The meanings of these interpretations are close to each other. Al-Qurtubi: 12/109.\nWhat will the servant gain if he is constantly grateful to Allah, the Almighty?\nوَإِذۡ تَأَذَّنَ رَبُّكُمۡ لَئِن شَكَرۡتُمۡ لَأَزِيدَنَّكُمۡۖ وَلَئِن كَفَرۡتُمۡ إِنَّ عَذَابِي لَشَدِيدٞ ٧\n(If you are grateful), in Arabic, the word (grateful) is affirmed since human souls are inclined to being ungrateful. (I will surely give you more) from My favors, as gratitude secures existing favors and brings forth missing ones. Al-Biqai: 4/172.\nWhat is the benefit of being grateful for the favors?\nوَقَالَ مُوسَىٰٓ إِن تَكۡفُرُوٓاْ أَنتُمۡ وَمَن فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ جَمِيعٗا فَإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَغَنِيٌّ حَمِيدٌ ٨\nWhen one enjoins something and rewards for doing it, and forbids something and punishes for doing it, it is often for a benefit to him. Allah makes clear that He is way above any gain or harm that would result from either their faith or disbelief. The benefit and harm are exclusive to the servant. Al-Biqai: 4/172.\nWhat is the lesson learned from this verse?\nوَقَالَ مُوسَىٰٓ إِن تَكۡفُرُوٓاْ أَنتُمۡ وَمَن فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ جَمِيعٗا فَإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَغَنِيٌّ حَمِيدٌ ٨\nThe significance of this verse stems from the fact that most disbelievers think that they are doing Allah a favor by accepting the faith, and that their Prophets would personally benefit from urging them to accept the faith. So, when Allah promised them more for their gratitude, and warned them of punishment for their ingratitude, it is likely that they would think there is a benefit or harm that would reach Allah because of that. Therefore, Allah alerts them to this devilish whisper so that they would not be conceited about accepting the faith and renouncing disbelief. Ibn Ashur: 13/192.\nAllah is Free of need of His creation. What is the significance of this fact?\nجَآءَتۡهُمۡ رُسُلُهُم بِٱلۡبَيِّنَٰتِ فَرَدُّوٓاْ أَيۡدِيَهُمۡ فِيٓ أَفۡوَٰهِهِمۡ وَقَالُوٓاْ إِنَّا كَفَرۡنَا بِمَآ أُرۡسِلۡتُم بِهِۦ وَإِنَّا لَفِي شَكّٖ مِّمَّا تَدۡعُونَنَآ إِلَيۡهِ مُرِيبٖ ٩\n(But they returned their hands to their mouths), there are three explanations for this verse, first: The disbelievers returned their hands to their own mouths in rage, as Allah says, (they bite their fingertips at you in rage) [3:119]; or they did it in ridicule and laughter like one who would cover his mouth with his hand while laughing. Second: The disbelievers returned their hands to their own mouths signaling for the Prophets to be silent. Third: The disbelievers returned their hands to the Prophets' mouths to silence them. Ibn Juzay: 1/442\nFor one who calls to Allah, what is the lesson learned from the attitudes of misguided nations toward their Messengers?\nقَالَتۡ رُسُلُهُمۡ أَفِي ٱللَّهِ شَكّٞ\nCan there be any doubt about the existence of Allah? Human natural dispositions vouch for His existence, and they are naturally inclined toward affirming this fact because recognizing Allah's existence is deemed necessary to the human true nature. Ibn Kathir: 2/506.\nThe Messengers were appalled by the doubts about Allah's existence. Why?\nwords\nيَسُومُونَكُمThey afflict you\nتَأَذَّنَHe declared\nفَرَدُّوا أَيدِيَهُم فِي أَفوَاهِهِمThe bit their own hands in rage at the Messengers and religion\nفَاطِرِThe Creator"],[257,"§Ibrahim\ndeeds\nHumble yourself to Allah and ask him to grant you knowledge, the ability to do good, wisdom and success that He has conferred upon the righteous.\nSupplicate Allah to destroy the wrongdoers by the wrongdoers, and save Muslims.\nAssess your good deeds before you lose them on the Day of Resurrection; have they been marred with insincerity, shirk, or innovation?\nguid\nKnow that one of the important duties of the preacher is to have certain faith in the promise of Allah and rely upon Him, Glory be to Him.\nAllah promised the believers dwelling in the land after they were weak and humiliated, and this came true for the Companions (j) and their followers.\nShirk nullifies good deeds, so their doer does not reap the benefits on the Day of Resurrection.\nrefl\nقَالَتۡ لَهُمۡ رُسُلُهُمۡ إِن نَّحۡنُ إِلَّا بَشَرٞ مِّثۡلُكُمۡ وَلَٰكِنَّ ٱللَّهَ يَمُنُّ عَلَىٰ مَن يَشَآءُ مِنۡ عِبَادِهِۦۖ\n(But Allah confers favor upon whom He wills of His servants), Allah bestows His bounty upon him by giving him success, wisdom, knowledge and guidance. Al-Qurtubi: 12/115.\nParity in shape and appearance do not necessarily reflect the same in knowledge and wisdom. Explain in light of this verse.\nوَمَا لَنَآ أَلَّا نَتَوَكَّلَ عَلَى ٱللَّهِ وَقَدۡ هَدَىٰنَا سُبُلَنَاۚ وَلَنَصۡبِرَنَّ عَلَىٰ مَآ ءَاذَيۡتُمُونَاۚ وَعَلَى ٱللَّهِ فَلۡيَتَوَكَّلِ ٱلۡمُتَوَكِّلُونَ ١٢\nIt should be noted that the Messengers' trust in Allah was for the noblest and most sublime of aims, for they relied upon Him to establish and support His religion, guide His servants and save them from misguidance. This is the most perfect kind of reliance upon Allah. Al-Saadi: 423.\nWhat is the highest and most perfect level of reliance upon Allah?\nوَقَالَ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ لِرُسُلِهِمۡ لَنُخۡرِجَنَّكُم مِّنۡ أَرۡضِنَآ أَوۡ لَتَعُودُنَّ فِي مِلَّتِنَاۖ فَأَوۡحَىٰٓ إِلَيۡهِمۡ رَبُّهُمۡ لَنُهۡلِكَنَّ ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَ ١٣\nThe disbelievers gave their Messengers a choice between returning to their false religion or be driven out of the land. This is Allah’s way with His Messengers and servants to which He says: (Indeed, they were about to provoke you so as to drive you out of the land) [17:76]. Al-Qurtubi: 12/116.\nIs driving those who call to Allah from their land a new or an old habit of tyrants?\nوَلَنُسۡكِنَنَّكُمُ ٱلۡأَرۡضَ مِنۢ بَعۡدِهِمۡۚ ذَٰلِكَ لِمَنۡ خَافَ مَقَامِي وَخَافَ وَعِيدِ ١٤\n(This is for him who fears standing before Me and fears My threat) combining these two indicates that it is right for the believer to fear his Lord's wrath and His warning. Those who do are indeed pious and righteous. Ibn Ashur: 13/208.\nThis verse mentions an attribute of the believers. What is it?\nوَٱسۡتَفۡتَحُواْ وَخَابَ كُلُّ جَبَّارٍ عَنِيدٖ ١٥\nA tyrant is the arrogant who does not recognize a favor of anyone upon him. Obstinate is the stubborn with hardheaded approach against the truth and evades it. Al-Qurtubi: 12/117.\nWho, among people, is more likely to be doomed?\nوَيَأۡتِيهِ ٱلۡمَوۡتُ مِن كُلِّ مَكَانٖ\nIbrahim At-Taymi said: \"Death will come to him from every part of his body, even from the tips of his hair due to the pain he feels in every part of his body.\" Ad-Dhahhak said: \"Death will come to him from everywhere, even from his toes.\" Al-Qurtubi: 12/122.\nHow will death come from everywhere to the tyrants in Hellfire? What proves that?\nمَّثَلُ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ بِرَبِّهِمۡۖ أَعۡمَٰلُهُمۡ كَرَمَادٍ ٱشۡتَدَّتۡ بِهِ ٱلرِّيحُ فِي يَوۡمٍ عَاصِفٖۖ لَّا يَقۡدِرُونَ مِمَّا كَسَبُواْ عَلَىٰ شَيۡءٖۚ ذَٰلِكَ هُوَ ٱلضَّلَٰلُ ٱلۡبَعِيدُ ١٨\nTheir work and deeds were not based on firm, correct grounds, and thus, they lost their rewards when they needed them the most. Ibn Kathir: 2/508.\nIn light of this verse, show the risk of being easy with religious innovation and shirk?\nwords\nمَقَامِيStanding before Me for reckoning\nوَاستَفتَحُواThe Messengers asked Allah for victory\nوَخَابَHe was doomed\nصَدِيدٍThe oozes from the skins of inhabitants of the Fire\nيَتَجَرَّعُهُHe can hardly swallow it"],[258,"§Ibrahim\ndeeds\nDo not feel secure from satan, and seek refuge with Allah from him often, for he is a cause of every trial.\nSit in a session by yourself for reckoning and reviewing of your past deeds.\nRead an explanation of the word of Tawhīd (there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah), its conditions and pillars, and reflect on its meanings.\nguid\nThe position of the weak with regard to the arrogant on the Day of Resurrection makes you never pamper anyone at the expense of religious matters, and impels you to follow Sharia not individuals.\nThe most thing the polytheists wish for on the Day of Resurrection is guidance, so strive for it in this worldly life, now that you can.\nBear patiently with doing good deeds, and abstain from committing sins before a Day comes in which no patience nor cry will be of benefit.\nrefl\nأَلَمۡ تَرَ أَنَّ ٱللَّهَ خَلَقَ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلۡأَرۡضَ بِٱلۡحَقِّۚ إِن يَشَأۡ يُذۡهِبۡكُمۡ وَيَأۡتِ بِخَلۡقٖ جَدِيدٖ ١٩\n(If He wills, He can do away with you and produce a new creation), He is capable of obliterating as He is of creating things, so do not disobey Him, for if you do (He can do away with you and produce a new creation) who are better and more obedient than you are. Al-Qurtubi: 12/125.\nWhat is the punishment that would strike us if we disobey Allah and follow our whims?\nوَقَالَ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنُ لَمَّا قُضِيَ ٱلۡأَمۡرُ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ وَعَدَكُمۡ وَعۡدَ ٱلۡحَقِّ\nIblis, may Allah curse him, will stand and address his followers in order to add sorrow to their sorrow, a deprivation to their deprivation, and regret to their regret. Ibn Kathir: 2/510\nWhat is the aim of Iblis's address to the people of Hellfire?\nوَقَالَ ٱلشَّيۡطَٰنُ لَمَّا قُضِيَ ٱلۡأَمۡرُ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ وَعَدَكُمۡ وَعۡدَ ٱلۡحَقِّ وَوَعَدتُّكُمۡ فَأَخۡلَفۡتُكُمۡۖ\nAllah states what satan will say on the Day of Judgment to alert the listeners, urge them to think about their end, to be ready for the inevitable, and visualize the setting at which satan will say that, so they become fearful and do what will benefit them then. Al-Alusi: 14/266.\nWhat is the wisdom behind informing us of what satan will say to his followers on the Day of Judgment?\nوَمَا كَانَ لِيَ عَلَيۡكُم مِّن سُلۡطَٰنٍ إِلَّآ أَن دَعَوۡتُكُمۡ فَٱسۡتَجَبۡتُمۡ لِيۖ\nThey are the ones who gave him this power over themselves, by taking him as an ally and joining his party. Hence, he has no power over those who believe and put their trust in their Lord. Al-Saadi: 425.\nWhat is the trait of one over whom Iblis has authority?\nوَمَا كَانَ لِيَ عَلَيۡكُم مِّن سُلۡطَٰنٍ إِلَّآ أَن دَعَوۡتُكُمۡ فَٱسۡتَجَبۡتُمۡ لِيۖ\nIt should be noted that in this verse, Allah states that satan has no power, and elsewhere He says: (His authority is only over those who take him as an ally and those who through him associate others with Allah) [16:100]. The power which Allah tells us that satan does not possess is the power of proof and evidence. He has no proof at all for that to which he calls people. All that he has is specious arguments that he presents to make falsehood fair-seeming, so that people will have justification in their minds to commit sin. As for the power which Allah tells us that satan has, it is the power by means of tempting his allies to commit sin; he strongly incites them to commit sin. Al-Saadi: 425.\nIblis's authority is negated in one verse and confirmed in another. How can you reconcile the two verses?\nتَحِيَّتُهُمۡ فِيهَا سَلَٰمٌ ٢٣\nThey greet each other by saying: \"Peace\" (salam), and the angels greet them by the same. Al-Qurtubi: 2/555.\nSaying \"Peace\" is the best greeting. What is the proof of that?\nأَلَمۡ تَرَ كَيۡفَ ضَرَبَ ٱللَّهُ مَثَلٗا كَلِمَةٗ طَيِّبَةٗ كَشَجَرَةٖ طَيِّبَةٍ أَصۡلُهَا ثَابِتٞ وَفَرۡعُهَا فِي ٱلسَّمَآءِ ٢٤\nThe good word: Tawhīd (there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah). It is like a tree, and the good deeds are its fruits at all times. Ibn Taimyah: 4/110.\nThe good word is Tawhīd and the good deeds are its fruits. Explain.\nwords\nسَوَاءٌ عَلَينَاIt is all the same for us\nمَحِيصٍAn escape\nسُلطَانٍAuthority, power\nبِمُصرِخِكُمBe called to your aid\nكَفَرتُI deny"],[259,"§Ibrahim\ndeeds\nUse an example in your speech today, for it is effective in conveying your message.\nSay, \"O Allah, keep me steadfast with the firm Word, in worldly life and in the Hereafter.\"\nEstablish the five daily prayers in congregation.\nguid\nSteadfastness can be in this worldly life and in the Hereafter, and it is a favor from Allah, and whom He keeps steadfast in this life, will keep him steadfast in the Hereafter.\nWrongdoing is a cause for being led astray by Allah, the Almighty, so avoid wrongdoing especially against the weak from among women, orphans, servants, daily workers and the needy.\nA wise person knows the truth of life enjoyment, and that it is perishable, so he is not distracted by it from working for the Hereafter.\nrefl\nتُؤۡتِيٓ أُكُلَهَا كُلَّ حِينِۢ بِإِذۡنِ رَبِّهَاۗ\nThe wisdom in comparing faith to a tree is that a tree has to have three things to be a tree: A firm root, a standing trunk and high branches; similarly, faith is not complete without these three things: Acceptance by the heart, statement by the tongue, and action by deeds. Al-Baghawi: 2/556.\nWhat is the wisdom in comparing the servant's faith to a tree?\nيُثَبِّتُ ٱللَّهُ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ بِٱلۡقَوۡلِ ٱلثَّابِتِ فِي ٱلۡحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنۡيَا\nAllah will make them steadfast in the life of this world, when they are faced with specious arguments and doubts, He guides them to certainty; when they are tempted by desires, He bestows upon them strong resolve whereby they will give precedence to that which Allah loves over their own whims and desires. Al-Saadi: 425.\nGive some examples of how Allah makes His servant steadfast in worldly life.\nيُثَبِّتُ ٱللَّهُ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ بِٱلۡقَوۡلِ ٱلثَّابِتِ فِي ٱلۡحَيَوٰةِ ٱلدُّنۡيَا وَفِي ٱلۡأٓخِرَةِۖ\nAllah will make them steadfast at the end of life, at the moment of death, He will make them steadfast in their Islamic religion and give them a good end; in the grave, when they are questioned by the two angels, He will guide them to the correct answer. Al-Saadi: 426.\nGive some examples of how Allah makes His servant steadfast at the end of life and beyond.\nوَيُضِلُّ ٱللَّهُ ٱلظَّٰلِمِينَۚ وَيَفۡعَلُ ٱللَّهُ مَا يَشَآءُ ٢٧\nIn recompense for their disbelief in this worldly life, Allah does not guide the disbelievers to the right answer when they are questioned in their graves by the two angels. When they are asked, they would say: \"we do not know,\", the angels reply: \"you neither knew nor recited [the Quran]\", so then he is hit with maces. Al-Qurtubi: 12/140.\nHow are the wrongdoers sent astray after their death?\nأَلَمۡ تَرَ إِلَى ٱلَّذِينَ بَدَّلُواْ نِعۡمَتَ ٱللَّهِ كُفۡرٗا وَأَحَلُّواْ قَوۡمَهُمۡ دَارَ ٱلۡبَوَارِ ٢٨\nWhoever searches into the affairs of this world, will conclude that Allah did not bestow a greater blessing upon people of the earth than sending them His Messengers, but the ones rejected His message are those of whom Allah says: (Did you not see those who exchanged Allah's blessings with disbelief, and led their people to the abode of ruin). Ibn Taimyah: 4/116-117.\nAllah did not bestow a greater favor upon His creation than sending them the Message of Muhammad (ﷺ). How?\nقُلۡ تَمَتَّعُواْ فَإِنَّ مَصِيرَكُمۡ إِلَى ٱلنَّارِ ٣٠\n(Say, \"Enjoy yourselves\"): This is a threat to them, which belittles their pleasures in this worldly life since they are brief. Al-Qurtubi: 12/142.\nThe adornment of this worldly life is called passing enjoyment. Why?\nقُل لِّعِبَادِيَ ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُواْ يُقِيمُواْ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ\nEstablishing prayer means performing it on time, fulfilling its conditions while maintaining humility throughout its acts of bowing and prostrations. Ibn Kathir: 2/519.\nWhat is meant by establishing prayer in this verse?\nwords\nاجتُثَّتIt is uprooted\nقَرَارٍStability\nالبَوَارِDestruction\nخِلاَلٌFriendship\nدَائِبَينِThey orbit continuously"],[260,"§Ibrahim\ndeeds\nRecall an unjust act that you inflicted onto someone, and rectify it with him before you wish you had but cannot.\nSupplicate Allah with these supplications of Abraham (u)\nSupplicate Allah to grant you righteous offspring.\nguid\nYou cannot count Allah's blessings upon you, much less thank Him for them, but keep your tongue wet with the remembrance of Allah and keen on thanking Him.\nThe ties of faith and Tawhīd take precedence over ties of blood and kinship.\nMaintaining the security of the society is one of the first wishes of the righteous and preachers.\nrefl\nوَءَاتَىٰكُم مِّن كُلِّ مَا سَأَلۡتُمُوهُۚ وَإِن تَعُدُّواْ نِعۡمَتَ ٱللَّهِ لَا تُحۡصُوهَآۗ\n(You cannot count them), you cannot bear counting them, and you will never be able to, because of their abundance, such as the hearing, the sight, and good body form in addition to others, like health and sustenance; they are countless blessings. Al-Qurtubi: 12/145.\nCan you bear count Allah's blessings upon you? Why?\nوَإِذۡ قَالَ إِبۡرَٰهِيمُ رَبِّ ٱجۡعَلۡ هَٰذَا ٱلۡبَلَدَ ءَامِنٗا\nAllah answered his supplication by making Makkah a sacred place in Sharia, and ordained measures to protect its sanctity, as it is well known, to the extent that no wrongdoer ever intended evil for it but Allah destroyed him, as He did with the people of the Elephant and others. Al-Saadi: 426.\nGive examples of how Allah answered the supplication of Abraham (u)?\nوَمَنۡ عَصَانِي فَإِنَّكَ غَفُورٞ رَّحِيمٞ ٣٦\nThis is an example of the compassion of Abraham (u) as he prayed for forgiveness and mercy from Allah for the sinners. Al-Saadi: 427.\nGive an example of the compassion of the Prophets for their people. How can a preacher benefit from this?\nرَبَّنَا لِيُقِيمُواْ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ\nMeaning: Make them a people who affirm Your Oneness and establish prayer, for establishing prayer is one of the most important and most virtuous acts of worship; whoever establishes prayer has established his religion. Al-Saadi: 427.\nIn his supplication for his offspring, Abraham (u) singled out prayer for mention from among all acts of worship. Why?\nٱلۡحَمۡدُ لِلَّهِ ٱلَّذِي وَهَبَ لِي عَلَى ٱلۡكِبَرِ إِسۡمَٰعِيلَ وَإِسۡحَٰقَۚ إِنَّ رَبِّي لَسَمِيعُ ٱلدُّعَآءِ ٣٩\nIn praising Allah, Abraham (u) said, (Indeed, my Lord is the All-Hearing of prayers), the mentioned (Hearing) here is the special one which is that of acceptance and response to the supplication, not the general hearing since Allah hears everything. Ibn Taimyah: 4/120.\nIn praising Allah, Abraham (u) singled out for mention the Hearing of Allah, even though Allah hears everything. Why?\nوَلَا تَحۡسَبَنَّ ٱللَّهَ غَٰفِلًا عَمَّا يَعۡمَلُ ٱلظَّٰلِمُونَۚ إِنَّمَا يُؤَخِّرُهُمۡ لِيَوۡمٖ تَشۡخَصُ فِيهِ ٱلۡأَبۡصَٰرُ ٤٢\nMeaning: Be patient as was Abraham, and inform the polytheists that delaying their punishment is not a sign of approval for their actions, rather it is Allah's way of giving the sinners respite. Maimun bin Mahran said: \"This is a threat to wrongdoer and a consolation to the oppressed.\" Al-Qurtubi: 12/157.\nIs delaying the punishment of the wrongdoer a sign of approval for his actions?\nإِنَّمَا يُؤَخِّرُهُمۡ لِيَوۡمٖ تَشۡخَصُ فِيهِ ٱلۡأَبۡصَٰرُ ٤٢\nThe eyes will not blink because of the intensity of the horrors and disturbing turmoil that they see. Al-Saadi: 427.\nWhat is the indication of having peoples eyes staring without blinking on the Day of Resurrection?\nwords\nتَهوِي إِلَيهِمIncline toward them\nتَشخَصُTheir eyes stare without blinking"],[261,"§Ibrahim\ndeeds\nShare a message in which you warn of Allah's punishment and the severity of his wrath.\nSeek refuge with Allah against the plot of the wrongdoers and say, \"O Allah, we make You our shield against them, and seek Your protection against their evil\" and say, \"O Allah, plot for us and do not plot against us.\"\nReflect on the story of a wrongdoer mentioned in the Quran, and how he planned a war against Allah's religion, then reflect on how his end was.\nguid\nWhile the tyrannical wrongdoer persists in his aggression in this world, he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection in fear and dread, his heart will be torn apart by horror.\nThe ancient ruins of punished nations serve only to remind people of the ordeal of eradication that befell the peoples who came before us.\nAllah will never fail in His promise to His messengers and allies, and victory and empowerment will definitely come to them.\nrefl\nمُهۡطِعِينَ مُقۡنِعِي رُءُوسِهِمۡ لَا يَرۡتَدُّ إِلَيۡهِمۡ طَرۡفُهُمۡۖ وَأَفۡـِٔدَتُهُمۡ هَوَآءٞ ٤٣\n(Rushing ahead), they will not turn their heads to the right or left, nor will they know on which their feet step. (Their glance does not come back to them), their eyes will not blink due to intensity of what they see, which will keep them distracted. (And their hearts are void), their hearts will leave their chests and reach their throats; not exiting through their mouths nor returning back. Al-Baghawi: 2/568.\nHave you seen wrongdoers, their toughness and hardened hearts against the believers in this world? Describe their condition on the Day of Resurrection.\nلَا يَرۡتَدُّ إِلَيۡهِمۡ طَرۡفُهُمۡۖ\nThey will stare continuously, and will not blink for an instant because they will be going through tremendous horror, worry, and fear of what is going to strike them. Ibn Kathir: 2/522.\nOn the Day of Resurrection, the wrongdoers will stare continuously and will not blink. Why?\nوَأَفۡـِٔدَتُهُمۡ هَوَآءٞ ٤٣\nMeaning: Their hearts are void of comprehension and understanding due to the immense bewilderment and astonishment. In Arabic, the word (void) is used to describe a person who is either a coward or a fool by saying: \"His heart is void\", which means he has no power nor a good mind. Al-Alusi: 14/310.\nHow does the heart become void?\nوَضَرَبۡنَا لَكُمُ ٱلۡأَمۡثَالَ ٤٥\nMeaning: The land of Thamud and akin to that; did you learn a lesson from their ruined dwellings after you saw what we did to them. Al-Qurtubi: 12/163.\nWhat do you say to one who passes by the ruined dwellings of perished people but does not learn a lesson from that?\nفَلَا تَحۡسَبَنَّ ٱللَّهَ مُخۡلِفَ وَعۡدِهِۦ رُسُلَهُۥٓۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ عَزِيزٞ ذُو ٱنتِقَامٖ ٤٧\n(So never think that Allah will fail in His promise to His messengers), which is the promise of defeating the disbelievers. In this verse, the promise is mentioned before the Messengers to indicate the absolute fulfillment of the promise. The Messengers are mentioned next to emphasize the fact that Allah never fails in His promise to anyone, let alone His Messengers who are the best among His creations. The promise is mentioned first to indicate absolute fulfillment, and the Messengers are mentioned next for their special status. Ibn Juzay: 1/448.\nIn this verse, the promise is mentioned before the Messengers (His promise to His messengers). Why?\nوَتَرَى ٱلۡمُجۡرِمِينَ يَوۡمَئِذٖ مُّقَرَّنِينَ فِي ٱلۡأَصۡفَادِ ٤٩\nEach disbeliever will be bound to his devil in a chain; moreover, it is said that their hands and feet will be bound to their necks in irons and shackles. Al-Baghawi: 2/571.\nDescribe how criminals will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection.\nإِنَّ ٱللَّهَ سَرِيعُ ٱلۡحِسَابِ ٥١\nFor Allah knows everything and nothing ever escapes His observation. Verily, His power over all of His creation is the same as His power over one creature. Ibn Kathir: 2/525.\nAllah's reckoning is described as swift. Why?\nwords\nمُهطِعِينَRushing ahead\nمُقنِعِي رُؤُوسِهِمTheir heads raised up\nوَأَفئِدَتُهُم هَوَاءٌTheir hearts are void due to immense horror\nمُقَرَّنِينَ فِي الأَصفَادِThey are bound in irons, their hands and feet are chained\nسَرَابِيلُهُمTheir garments"],[262,"§Al-Hijr\ndeeds\nThank Allah for guiding you to Islam, and pray to Allah, the Almighty, to make you firm upon it until you meet Him.\nVisit the graves and contemplate your fate, for visiting the graves is a Sunnah, and it is one of the things that keep the servant away from false hope.\nSet up a schedule in which you organize your time to help you set goals and do a continuous serious work.\nguid\nMovies and mobile entertainment applications distract one from good deeds.\nOne of the manifestations of Allah's mercy toward man is that man asks for torment but Allah bestows mercy.\nAs a punishment for sins, one will not able to benefit from the Quran when listening or reading it.\nrefl\nرُّبَمَا يَوَدُّ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُواْ لَوۡ كَانُواْ مُسۡلِمِينَ ٢\nAlhasan said: When the polytheists see the believers enter Paradise not Hellfire, they will wish that they had been Muslims. Al-Qurtubi: 12/176.\nWhen will the disbeliever wish that he had been a Muslim?\nذَرۡهُمۡ يَأۡكُلُواْ وَيَتَمَتَّعُواْ وَيُلۡهِهِمُ ٱلۡأَمَلُۖ فَسَوۡفَ يَعۡلَمُونَ ٣\nFalse hope is an incurable chronic disease, and when it settles in the heart, it becomes so corrupted that treatment and remedy will be of no use, and doctors and wise men will give up in despair. The reality of false hope is the greed and love for the adornments of this life and turning away from the life of the Hereafter. Al-Qurtubi: 12/189.\nWhat is the terrible disease against which Allah warned us in this verse?\nذَرۡهُمۡ يَأۡكُلُواْ وَيَتَمَتَّعُواْ وَيُلۡهِهِمُ ٱلۡأَمَلُۖ فَسَوۡفَ يَعۡلَمُونَ ٣\nIn this verse, there is an indication that pursuing joy and pleasures in this life while not being ready for the life of the Hereafter is not a trait of one who seeks salvation. Alhasan said: A servant who has false hope will do evil deeds. Ali bin Abi Talib (t) said: I fear for you two things, false hope and following whims; false hope causes you to forget the Hereafter, and following whims turns you away from the truth. Al-Alusi: 14/341.\nFalse hope results in many harms. Explain in light of this verse.\nلَّوۡ مَا تَأۡتِينَا بِٱلۡمَلَٰٓئِكَةِ إِن كُنتَ مِنَ ٱلصَّٰدِقِينَ ٧\nMeaning: Since you have not brought the angels, then you are not telling the truth. This was the ultimate unfairness and ignorance. As for being unfair, that is obvious, because this was insolence toward Allah and stubbornness in demanding specific signs that He had not chosen to send since the aim was achieved, and proof was established by means of many other signs that pointed to the soundness of the message He brought. As for ignorance, they could not differentiate between what was in their best interests and what was detrimental to their interests. There was nothing good for them in the angels coming down; rather, Allah does not send down the angels except for just cause, after which there is no respite for anyone who does not follow the truth or submit to it. Al-Saadi: 429.\nThere is unfairness and ignorance in their request to bring the angels. Explain.\nإِنَّا نَحۡنُ نَزَّلۡنَا ٱلذِّكۡرَ\nMeaning: In which there is a reminder of all things and clear proof, by means of which a person will be reminded if he wants to be reminded. Al-Saadi: 429.\nThe Quran is described as a (reminder). Why?\nإِنَّا نَحۡنُ نَزَّلۡنَا ٱلذِّكۡرَ وَإِنَّا لَهُۥ لَحَٰفِظُونَ ٩\nPreserving the Quran means protecting it against changes and distortion as it was done to the previous Scriptures. Allah protected the Quran so that no one could add, delete, or distort it in contrast to previous Scriptures of which their protection was entrusted to their followers as Allah says, (because they were entrusted to protect the Scripture of Allah) [5:44]. Ibn Juzay: 1/450.\nWhat is the difference between the Quran and the previous Scripters with respect to being preserved from change?\nمَا نُنَزِّلُ ٱلۡمَلَٰٓئِكَةَ إِلَّا بِٱلۡحَقِّ وَمَا كَانُوٓاْ إِذٗا مُّنظَرِينَ ٨\nMujahid said: The angels are sent down with either the Message or destruction. They are sent down to the Messengers with the true words, and to those who had been warned with the true actions of destruction or deliverance. Al-Biqai: 4/206.\nWhat is the truth for which the angels come down?\nwords\nوَيُلهِهِمُ الأَمَلُAnd be diverted with false hope\nلَو مَاWhy not\nشِيَعِ الأَوَّلِينَThe sects of the former peoples\nفَظَلُّواThey kept on\nيَعرُجُونَAscending\nسُكِّرَتAffected by magic"],[263,"§Al-Hijr\ndeeds\nDonate to a person in need, or to a voluntary institution, and do not fear abatement from the Lord of the Throne.\nPrecede others in performing an act of worship, as the forerunner will be among the first to enter Paradise.\nRead the story of Adam and satan from the Quranic interpretation books, then reflect on the points that satan exploited to influence Adam.\nguid\nContemplate the planets and stars in the sky; Allah has made them a sign and an ornament for the observers.\nContemplate the Earth, the way it is spread out, and the provisions it contains.\nDo not grieve over your limited sustenance; Allah knows what is best for you, and be content with what He has destined for you.\nrefl\nوَلَقَدۡ جَعَلۡنَا فِي ٱلسَّمَآءِ بُرُوجٗا وَزَيَّنَّٰهَا لِلنَّٰظِرِينَ ١٦\nThis calls the observers to reflect upon it, contemplate its significance, and see the indications of its Creator. Al-Saadi: 430.\nHow do great stars and their positions increase the believer's faith?\nوَٱلۡأَرۡضَ مَدَدۡنَٰهَا\nMeaning: We have made it spacious and have made both humans and animals able to move about, seeking their provision and settling in various spots. Al-Saadi: 430.\nThe belief that provisions on Earth will not suffice all the people in the future is considered a negative assumption about Allah. Explain in light of this verse.\nوَلَقَدۡ عَلِمۡنَا ٱلۡمُسۡتَقۡدِمِينَ مِنكُمۡ وَلَقَدۡ عَلِمۡنَا ٱلۡمُسۡتَـٔۡخِرِينَ ٢٤ وَإِنَّ رَبَّكَ هُوَ يَحۡشُرُهُمۡۚ إِنَّهُۥ حَكِيمٌ عَلِيمٞ ٢٥\n(And We have already known the preceding among you, and We have already known the later), the past and future generations of people. This is mentioned to indicate their gathering on the Last Day which is in the next verse, (and your Lord will gather them; indeed, He is Wise and Knowing), since He has encompassed them in knowledge, it will not be difficult for Him to resurrect and gather them. Ibn Juzay: 1/451.\nWhat is the link between these two verses: (And We have already known the preceding among you) and (and your Lord will gather them)?\nوَلَقَدۡ خَلَقۡنَا ٱلۡإِنسَٰنَ مِن صَلۡصَٰلٖ مِّنۡ حَمَإٖ مَّسۡنُونٖ ٢٦ وَٱلۡجَآنَّ خَلَقۡنَٰهُ مِن قَبۡلُ مِن نَّارِ ٱلسَّمُومِ ٢٧\nThe verse is intended to point out the noble nature, good essence and pure origin of Adam (u). Ibn Kathir: 2/531.\nThe creations of man and jinn are mentioned together. Why?\nفَإِذَا سَوَّيۡتُهُۥ وَنَفَخۡتُ فِيهِ مِن رُّوحِي فَقَعُواْ لَهُۥ سَٰجِدِينَ ٢٩\nCommanding the angels to prostrate to Adam (u) does not contradict the prohibition of prostrating to other than Allah in Islam for these points, First: The prohibition is placed to block the means to committing shirk, however, the angels are infallible, so shirk would not be possible. Second: Islamic Sharia has the distinction of reaching the highest limits of truth and goodness, hence its ordinances far exceed those of previous Sharias because Allah intends for its followers to attain optimal awareness. Third: This event occurred in the higher world of which its rules do not apply to our world. Ibn Ashur: 14/45.\nCommanding the angels to prostrate to Adam (u) does not contradict the prohibition of prostrating to other than Allah in Islam for some points. What are they?\nفَإِذَا سَوَّيۡتُهُۥ وَنَفَخۡتُ فِيهِ مِن رُّوحِي فَقَعُواْ لَهُۥ سَٰجِدِينَ ٢٩\nAdam (u) was created out of clay, and was honored because Allah had breathed into him of His spirit; this is why Allah says, (when I have shaped him and breathed into him of My spirit, then fall down before him in prostration), so the prostration was hinged on the breathing into him of Allah's spirit, hence the favoring of Adam (u) was due to this honor which Iblis does not have. Ibn Taimyah: 4/125.\nExplain the reason for favoring Adam (u) above others in light of this verse.\nفَسَجَدَ ٱلۡمَلَٰٓئِكَةُ كُلُّهُمۡ أَجۡمَعُونَ ٣٠ إِلَّآ إِبۡلِيسَ أَبَىٰٓ أَن يَكُونَ مَعَ ٱلسَّٰجِدِينَ ٣١\nHere, Allah mentions the blessings that He bestowed upon our father Adam (u) and what happened with his enemy Iblis, including a warning to us of his evil and temptation. Al-Saadi: 431.\nWhat is the aim of the detailed narration of the creation of Adam (u) and the stance of Iblis?\nwords\nبُرُوجًاPositions of planets\nرَجِيمٍExpelled from the mercy of Allah\nاستَرَقَ السمعOne who steals a hearing\nلَوَاقِحَWinds fertilize the clouds to be full of water\nصَلصَالٍDry clay\nحمإBlack mud\nمسنونAltered in smell and color\nنار السمومSmokeless and extremely hot fire"],[264,"§Al-Hijr\ndeeds\nIdentify a trick by which satan had deceived you, then think of a way out of it.\nAsk Allah to protect you from satan and make you among His chosen servants.\nForgive someone who had wronged or offended you, as that purifies your heart and comforts your soul.\nguid\nLove for others what you love for yourself, as that comforts your heart.\nOne of Iblis' most powerful weapons is alluring distractions and evil to people.\nIblis has no authority nor control over anyone except when a person allows him.\nrefl\nقَالَ لَمۡ أَكُن لِّأَسۡجُدَ لِبَشَرٍ خَلَقۡتَهُۥ مِن صَلۡصَٰلٖ مِّنۡ حَمَإٖ مَّسۡنُونٖ ٣٣\nAllah mentions how His enemy Iblis, amidst all the angels, refused to prostrate to Adam (u) out of envy, disbelief, stubbornness, arrogance, and false pride. Ibn Kathir: 2/531.\nEnvy and arrogance can lead one to extreme. Explain.\nقَالَ رَبِّ فَأَنظِرۡنِيٓ إِلَىٰ يَوۡمِ يُبۡعَثُونَ ٣٦ قَالَ فَإِنَّكَ مِنَ ٱلۡمُنظَرِينَ ٣٧\nThe divine response to his supplication was not an honor in his case; rather, it was a test and trial from Allah for him and for people, so that it might become clear who will be sincere and obey his Lord instead of his enemy and who will not. Al-Saadi: 431.\nWhat is explanation for Allah's response to Iblis' supplication?\nقَالَ رَبِّ بِمَآ أَغۡوَيۡتَنِي لَأُزَيِّنَنَّ لَهُمۡ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ وَلَأُغۡوِيَنَّهُمۡ أَجۡمَعِينَ ٣٩\nHere, The allurement of the devil comes in two ways, by making sins fair-seeming to them, or by distracting them with the adornments of this life from acts of obedience. Al-Qurtubi: 12/212.\nThe devil's alluring comes in two ways. What are they?\nقَالَ رَبِّ بِمَآ أَغۡوَيۡتَنِي لَأُزَيِّنَنَّ لَهُمۡ فِي ٱلۡأَرۡضِ وَلَأُغۡوِيَنَّهُمۡ أَجۡمَعِينَ ٣٩ إِلَّا عِبَادَكَ مِنۡهُمُ ٱلۡمُخۡلَصِينَ ٤٠ قَالَ هَٰذَا صِرَٰطٌ عَلَيَّ مُسۡتَقِيمٌ ٤١\nMeaning: Those whom You choose and select for their sincerity, faith and reliance upon You. Al-Saadi: 431.\nWho are those excluded from Iblis' alluring?\nإِنَّ عِبَادِي لَيۡسَ لَكَ عَلَيۡهِمۡ سُلۡطَٰنٌ إِلَّا مَنِ ٱتَّبَعَكَ مِنَ ٱلۡغَاوِينَ ٤٢\nIblis has no authority over those who are sincere and faithful, that is why devils run away from a house in which Surat Al-Baqarah, Ayatu Al-Kursi, the last verses of Surat Al-Baqarah, and other devil's striking verses in the Quran are recited. Ibn Taimyah: 4/131.\nThe verse mentions a group of people who are excluded from allurement of Iblis. Who are they? Specify two ways of driving the devil away.\nنَبِّئۡ عِبَادِيٓ أَنِّيٓ أَنَا ٱلۡغَفُورُ ٱلرَّحِيمُ ٤٩\nFor if they understand the perfect nature of His mercy and forgiveness, they will strive hard, taking all measures that could lead them to attain His mercy, and they will give up sin and repent therefrom, so that they may attain His forgiveness. Al-Saadi: 432.\nWhat is stance of the believer when he knows that Allah is All-Forgiving, the Most Merciful?\nنَبِّئۡ عِبَادِيٓ أَنِّيٓ أَنَا ٱلۡغَفُورُ ٱلرَّحِيمُ ٤٩ وَأَنَّ عَذَابِي هُوَ ٱلۡعَذَابُ ٱلۡأَلِيمُ ٥٠\nThe servant's heart should always be between fear and hope; when he thinks of the mercy, forgiveness, generosity and kindness of his Lord, that fills him with hope, but when he thinks of his sins and shortcomings with regard to his duties towards his Lord, that instils fear in him and makes him give up his sin. Al-Saadi: 432.\nHow should the believer's heart be in this worldly life?\nwords\nفَأَنظِرنِيGrant me respite\nصِرَاطٌPath\nسُلطَانٌAuthority\nبِسَلاَمٍSafe from all ills\nغِلٍّResentment\nنَصَبٌFatigue\nنَبّىInform"],[265,"§Al-Hijr\ndeeds\nBegin with greeting (salam) when entering a house, or when meeting a Muslim.\nGive good tidings to a Muslim today to make him rejoice and please his heart.\nGive a speech, or share a message in which you explain the risk of despairing of Allah's mercy.\nguid\nThe good news may come after the cessation of worldly means.\nMan's engagement in improving himself, his family, and those around will save him from the turbulence of this worldly life and the Hereafter.\nThere is no value for bonds of kinship and marriage without faith.\nrefl\nإِذۡ دَخَلُواْ عَلَيۡهِ فَقَالُواْ سَلَٰمٗا قَالَ إِنَّا مِنكُمۡ وَجِلُونَ ٥٢\nSince these guests arrived at the house at a peculiar time, he thought that they intended to harm him. Ibn Ashur: 14/58.\nWhy did Abraham (u) begin by saying: (Indeed, we are fearful of you)?\nقَالُواْ بَشَّرۡنَٰكَ بِٱلۡحَقِّ فَلَا تَكُن مِّنَ ٱلۡقَٰنِطِينَ ٥٥\nSince Abraham (ﷺ) was free from despairing of Allah's mercy, the angels admonishment to him was polite. They cautioned him not to be of those who despair. Ibn Ashur: 14/60.\nThe angels addressed Abraham (u) in a polite manner. Explain.\nقَالَ وَمَن يَقۡنَطُ مِن رَّحۡمَةِ رَبِّهِۦٓ إِلَّا ٱلضَّآلُّونَ ٥٦\nMeaning: Who despairs of his Lord's mercy (except for those astray), the losers. Despair of Allah's mercy is a major sin that is similar to feeling secure in His plan. Al-Baghawi: 2/590.\nSome sinners and those struck with afflictions become despair of Allah's mercy, saying: Allah will never forgive me! Or My affliction will never end! How do you respond to him?\nفَأَسۡرِ بِأَهۡلِكَ بِقِطۡعٖ مِّنَ ٱلَّيۡلِ وَٱتَّبِعۡ أَدۡبَٰرَهُمۡ وَلَا يَلۡتَفِتۡ مِنكُمۡ أَحَدٞ\nA common practice for leaders is to be closer to danger than others, sacrificing their souls and strengthening others; knowing that being closer to danger will not shorten their lives while being far from it will not save them from harm nor avail them against fate. Meaning: Follow behind them so that you will not worry about any of them being left behind, and that they will not look back out of respect to you. Al-Biqai: 4/229.\nWhen they left their city, Lot (u) walked behind his family. Why?\nفَأَسۡرِ بِأَهۡلِكَ بِقِطۡعٖ مِّنَ ٱلَّيۡلِ وَٱتَّبِعۡ أَدۡبَٰرَهُمۡ\nThey told him to walk behind them to protect them. Similarly, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would walk in the rear of the army on military campaigns, in order to help the weak and carry those who had no means of transport. Ibn Kathir: 2/535.\nDescribe the Sunnah of the Prophet (ﷺ) when marching for Jihad.\nوَلَا يَلۡتَفِتۡ مِنكُمۡ أَحَدٞ\nIn this case, the onlooker is unsettled because he is either uncertain of what Allah said or grieves over what is happening to them; thus, whoever looks back will be tormented. Moreover, walking without looking back reflects determination in migrating and prompts faster walking. Moreover, it shows that their hearts are no longer attached to their houses and belongings which they left behind, and that they do not grieve over those whom Allah's wrath had befallen. Even so, if they look back, they may see what they cannot bear to see. Al-Biqai: 4/229.\nWhat is the wisdom behind commanding Lot (u) and his family not to look back?\nوَٱتَّقُواْ ٱللَّهَ وَلَا تُخۡزُونِ ٦٩\nLot (u) reminded them using the religious deterrent -despite of their disbelief- thereby fulfilling the message he brought to them, and using the common deterrent, when he said, (And fear Allah and do not disgrace me). Ibn Ashur: 14/66.\nLot (u) reminded his people using the religious and common deterrents. Explain.\nwords\nوَجِلُونَWe are fearful, apprehensive\nالقَانِطِينَThose who despair\nفَمَا خَطبُكُمWhat is your mission?\nقَدَّرنَاWe decreed\nالغَابِرِينَThose who remain behind for punishment\nوَقَضَينَاWe revealed\nمَقطُوعٌObliterated by torment"],[266,"§Al-Hijr\ndeeds\nAsk Allah to grant you discernment, and pursue the means to attain it, which are fear of Allah and disobeying your whim.\nRead and contemplate Surat Al-Fatiha, then draw a valuable insight from each verse.\nTreat your Muslim brothers, especially servants and workers, with kindness.\nguid\nMan's obsession with the adornments of this worldly life can lead him to losing his mind.\nAllah keeps those whom He loves busy with His remembrance instead of being busy with worldly adornments.\nThe power of construction and crafting will not avail against the wrath of Allah.\nrefl\nإِنَّ فِي ذَٰلِكَ لَأٓيَٰتٖ لِّلۡمُتَوَسِّمِينَ ٧٥\nDiscernment can be attained through good mental ability, a sharp perception, a clear mind, and a heart that is devoid of the distractions of this worldly life, purified from the evil of sins, the tarnish of morals, and the longing for the adornments of this life. Al-Qurtubi: 12/234.\nHow can a servant attain true discernment?\nوَلَقَدۡ كَذَّبَ أَصۡحَٰبُ ٱلۡحِجۡرِ ٱلۡمُرۡسَلِينَ ٨٠\nThe Dwellers of Al-Hijr were the people of Thamud who denied their Prophet, Salih (u), and whoever denies one Messenger, denies all the Messengers. Thus they are described as denied (the Messengers). Ibn Kathir: 2/536.\nHow did the Dwellers of Al-Hijr deny all the Messengers even though they had only denied their Prophet, Salih (u)?\nفَمَآ أَغۡنَىٰ عَنۡهُم مَّا كَانُواْ يَكۡسِبُونَ ٨٤\nMeaning: Nothing avails them of what they had earned of wealth, fortresses in the mountains, and not even their own great physical power given to them by Allah. Al-Qurtubi: 12/249.\nCan wealth and material power ward off Allah’s punishment form a person or a community?\nفَٱصۡفَحِ ٱلصَّفۡحَ ٱلۡجَمِيلَ ٨٥\nAs opposed to forgiveness that is not gracious, which is inappropriate forgiveness. So, one should not be forgiving when punishment is more appropriate, such as punishment for transgressors and wrongdoers for whom nothing is effective except punishment. Al-Saadi: 434.\nIs there forgiveness that is not gracious? What is it?\nوَلَقَدۡ ءَاتَيۡنَٰكَ سَبۡعٗا مِّنَ ٱلۡمَثَانِي وَٱلۡقُرۡءَانَ ٱلۡعَظِيمَ ٨٧\nAbu Saeed bin Al-Mu'alla said: Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said: \"It is Surat Al-Fatiha, (Praise be to Allah, the Lord of the worlds) is the seven oft-repeated verses and the mighty Quran which I have been given.\" Al-Alusi: 14/432.\nWhat are the seven oft-repeated verses mentioned in this verse?\nلَا تَمُدَّنَّ عَيۡنَيۡكَ إِلَىٰ مَا مَتَّعۡنَا بِهِۦٓ أَزۡوَٰجٗا مِّنۡهُمۡ وَلَا تَحۡزَنۡ عَلَيۡهِمۡ وَٱخۡفِضۡ جَنَاحَكَ لِلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ ٨٨\n(Do not look longingly), do not look at the enjoyment We gave them in this life, as if saying: We have given you the seven of the oft-repeated verses and the great Quran, so do not look at this life because what We have given you is much greater. Ibn Juzay: 1/455.\nThis verse contains an approach for the purification of one’s soul, which has several recommendations. Explain.\nوَٱخۡفِضۡ جَنَاحَكَ لِلۡمُؤۡمِنِينَ ٨٨\nMeaning: Soften your conduct with those who followed you, and be humble with them. In the original text, the word \"wing\" is used as an image of a bird lowering its and hugs its young, which is a description of a man bringing his followers closer. Al-Qurtubi: 12/254.\nHow should the believer treat his faithful brethren?\nwords\nلَعَمرُكَAllah swears by the life of our Prophet (ﷺ)\nسَكرَتِهِمTheir heedlessness\nيَعمَهُونَWandering blindly\nلِلمُتَوَسِّمِينَFor those who discern and take warning\nالمُقتَسِمِينَThose who divided the Quran, believed in some parts of it and denied others"],[267,"§Al-Hijr, An-Nahl\ndeeds\nPartake in enjoining good or forbidding evil with people from your circle.\nRecord the blessings mentioned in Surah An-Nahl, then reflect on them until you realize the purpose of this Surah, which is the enumeration of blessings.\nRead about the minor and major signs of the Hour (Last Day).\nguid\nIt is important to declare the truth and clarify it, especially when there is no persecution or harm that outweighs the benefit of speaking the truth.\nGlorification and prostration reassure the heart and remove distress and anxiety from the soul.\nWorshiping Allah continues until the end of life.\nrefl\nفَوَرَبِّكَ لَنَسۡـَٔلَنَّهُمۡ أَجۡمَعِينَ ٩٢ عَمَّا كَانُواْ يَعۡمَلُونَ ٩٣\nIbn Abbas (t) said: \"Allah will not question them whether they did this or that because He is the All-Knowing, rather, that questioning is a scathing rebuke to them.\" Al-Qurtubi: 12/260.\nWhat type of questioning Allah will direct to the disbelievers on the Day of Resurrection?\nإِنَّا كَفَيۡنَٰكَ ٱلۡمُسۡتَهۡزِءِينَ ٩٥\nThis is a promise from Allah to His Messenger (ﷺ) that those who ridiculed him would not be able to harm him, and that Allah would suffice him against them by means of whatever kinds of punishment He willed. And He did indeed do that, for no one openly ridiculed the Messenger of Allah and the message he brought, but Allah destroyed him and caused him to die in the worst manner. Al-Saadi: 435.\nAllah promised His Messenger (ﷺ) that He would suffice him against the mockers. How is that done? What is Sharia rule on those who mock Allah’s Messenger (ﷺ)?\nإِنَّا كَفَيۡنَٰكَ ٱلۡمُسۡتَهۡزِءِينَ ٩٥ ٱلَّذِينَ يَجۡعَلُونَ مَعَ ٱللَّهِ إِلَٰهًا ءَاخَرَۚ فَسَوۡفَ يَعۡلَمُونَ ٩٦\nAllah describes those mockers as polytheists to console His Messenger (ﷺ) and lessen his distress by informing him that they had committed even a greater sin by their shirk. Al-Alusi: 14/441.\nAfter informing His Messenger that He would suffice him against the mockers, Allah describes the mockers as polytheists, what is the lesson in that?\nوَٱعۡبُدۡ رَبَّكَ حَتَّىٰ يَأۡتِيَكَ ٱلۡيَقِينُ ٩٩\nOmar bin Abdulaziz used to say: \"I have not seen a certain matter which is so similar to a doubtful one like the people certainty of death, yet they do not prepare themselves for it.\" It means that they act as if it is a doubtful matter. Al-Qurtubi: 12/265.\nAllah calls death (certainty), what is the lesson in this for the believer?\nأَتَىٰٓ أَمۡرُ ٱللَّهِ\nIn the Arabic text, Allah is informing us about the approach of the Hour (Last Day) in the past tense form in order to confirm that it will undoubtedly come to pass. Ibn Kathir: 2/541.\nAllah is informing about the approach of the Hour (Last Day) in the past tense. Why? What is the lesson in this for the believer?\nيُنَزِّلُ ٱلۡمَلَٰٓئِكَةَ بِٱلرُّوحِ مِنۡ أَمۡرِهِۦ عَلَىٰ مَن يَشَآءُ مِنۡ عِبَادِهِۦٓ\nIn the Arabic text, the word \"soul/spirit\" is used for revelation. It is called so because it breathes life into people's hearts. Al-Baghawi: 2/604.\nAllah calls His revelation a \"soul/spirit\". Why?\nوَٱلۡأَنۡعَٰمَ خَلَقَهَاۖ لَكُمۡ فِيهَا دِفۡءٞ وَمَنَٰفِعُ وَمِنۡهَا تَأۡكُلُونَ ٥ وَلَكُمۡ فِيهَا جَمَالٌ حِينَ تُرِيحُونَ وَحِينَ تَسۡرَحُونَ ٦\nThis Surah is called the Surah of blessings, because in the beginning Allah mentions the basic blessings, and at the end of it He mentions other blessings that complete those basic ones. Al-Saadi: 435-436.\nSurat An-Nahl is called Surah of the blessings. Why?\nwords\nعِضِينَPortions; some said: magic, others said: conjecture, etc.\nفَاصدَعDeclare\nبِالرُّوحِWith revelation\nخَصِيمٌA clear adversary\nتُرِيحُونYou bring them home to rest in the evening\nتَسرَحُونَYou take them out to graze in the morning"],[268,"§An-Nahl\ndeeds\nCount three blessings of means of transport bestowed upon us from Allah, then give thanks to Him.\nWhen riding an animal say, \"In the Name of Allah, all praise is due to Allah, Glory is to Him Who has subjected this to us, and we were not able to do it. And, surely, to our Lord are we returning.\"\nThink about the different fruits that grow yet they are all watered with the same water, then thank Allah for His blessings.\nguid\nOne of greatest blessings from Allah, the Almighty, upon his servants is the sending off rain from the skies, which gives life to everything.\nThe stars do not control themselves, so it is more appropriate that they neither harm nor benefit others, thus, it is to Allah, Glory be to Him, that supplication is directed.\nBe a grateful servant; whenever you receive a blessing, thank Allah for it.\nrefl\nوَٱلۡخَيۡلَ وَٱلۡبِغَالَ وَٱلۡحَمِيرَ لِتَرۡكَبُوهَا وَزِينَةٗۚ\nMeaning: Sometimes you use them for necessary purposes, such as riding, and sometimes you use them for the sake of beauty and adornment. No mention is made of eating because it is prohibited to eat mules and donkeys; horses are not usually used as food. Al-Saadi: 436.\nWhy is eating not mentioned as a benefit of these animals?\nوَٱلۡخَيۡلَ وَٱلۡبِغَالَ وَٱلۡحَمِيرَ لِتَرۡكَبُوهَا وَزِينَةٗۚ وَيَخۡلُقُ مَا لَا تَعۡلَمُونَ ٨\n(And He creates other things that you do not know), which would come about after the revelation of the Quran, in which people ride on land, sea, and air, and that they use for their own benefit and in their interests. They are not mentioned in specific terms because Allah does not mention in His Book anything but what people know, or they know something similar to it. As for that which they had no comparison, if He had mentioned them they would not have known them or understood what was meant by them. Thus, He mentions that in very general terms which may include what they know and what they do not know. The same may be said concerning the way in which He mentions the blessings of Paradise; He mentions by name those which we know or see something similar, such as palm trees, grapes and pomegranates, and He refers in general terms to those of which we know no comparison. Al-Saadi: 436.\nIn light of this verse, what is the style of the Quran in describing the unseen blessings?\nوَٱلۡخَيۡلَ وَٱلۡبِغَالَ وَٱلۡحَمِيرَ لِتَرۡكَبُوهَا وَزِينَةٗۚ وَيَخۡلُقُ مَا لَا تَعۡلَمُونَ ٨ وَعَلَى ٱللَّهِ قَصۡدُ ٱلسَّبِيلِ وَمِنۡهَا جَآئِرٞۚ وَلَوۡ شَآءَ لَهَدَىٰكُمۡ أَجۡمَعِينَ ٩\nWhen Allah mentioned the animals that may be used for the purpose of physical journeys, He also referred to the moral and religious routes that people may follow. Often in the Quran, there is a shift from physical or tangible things to beneficial spiritual and religious matters. Ibn Kathir: 2/544.\nWhat is the link between the above-mentioned verses?\nوَعَلَى ٱللَّهِ قَصۡدُ ٱلسَّبِيلِ وَمِنۡهَا جَآئِرٞۚ وَلَوۡ شَآءَ لَهَدَىٰكُمۡ أَجۡمَعِينَ ٩\nWhen Allah mentions easing the ways for people to reach their material objectives, He reminds of the ways that lead to the spiritual objective which is the path to guidance Thus, His caring to show the ways to the path of guidance is a greater blessing than easing the ways to material objectives, as the path of guidance leads to eternal pleasure. Ibn Ashur: 14/112.\nWhich is a greater blessing: The material or the spiritual one? Why?\nوَعَلَى ٱللَّهِ قَصۡدُ ٱلسَّبِيلِ وَمِنۡهَا جَآئِرٞۚ وَلَوۡ شَآءَ لَهَدَىٰكُمۡ أَجۡمَعِينَ ٩\n(It is upon Allah to show the straight path), it is upon Allah to show the way to guidance by presenting the evidence, and sending of messengers. Ibn Juzay: 1/459.\nAllah’s mercy is indicated in this verse. Explain.\nوَهُوَ ٱلَّذِي سَخَّرَ ٱلۡبَحۡرَ لِتَأۡكُلُواْ مِنۡهُ لَحۡمٗا طَرِيّٗا وَتَسۡتَخۡرِجُواْ مِنۡهُ حِلۡيَةٗ تَلۡبَسُونَهَاۖ\nSubjection of the sea is enabling people to use it for ferrying and docking, which is a blessing from Allah upon us, but if He had willed, He could have empowered the sea to drown us. Al-Qurtubi: 12/294.\nDescribe Allah's blessing in subjection of the sea for people.\nوَتَرَى ٱلۡفُلۡكَ مَوَاخِرَ فِيهِ وَلِتَبۡتَغُواْ مِن فَضۡلِهِۦ\n(And you see the ships cleaving their way through its waves): Qatadah said: You can see two ships, one is coming while another is leaving, and both are driven by the same wind. Al-Baghawi: 2/608.\nExplain the great blessing and power of Allah in subjecting the ships in the sea.\nwords\nأَثقَالَكُمYour heavy loads\nجَائِرٌDeviant\nفِيهِ تُسِيمُونَOn which you pasture your livestock\nذَرَأَHe has created\nمَوَاخِرَ فِيهِThe ships cleaving their way through its waves"]])